 Surgical Oncology faculty, we recommended a <1>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</1> strategy followed by ***** his surgical prospects. He initiated ***** on 03/06/2022, once his <2>LFTs</2> had sufficiently normalized post-<3>stent</3>, and is now s/p 3 cycles of <4>treatment</4>.    The patient's present review of systems was reviewed. He continues to tolerate <5>chemotherapy</5> quite well overall; his last cycle in fact was a/w less <6>hiccups</6>, <7>fatigue</7>, and <8>cold sensitivity</8>/<9>peripheral sensory neuropathy</9> than previously. He reports maintenance of a good appetite, and no <10>abdominal pain</10>, <11>diarrhea</11>, <12>fevers</12> or <13>chills</13>. He is staying active, walking and still playing golf.      PAST MEDICAL AND SURGICAL HISTORY  <14>Fatty liver disease</14>  <15>Chronic rhinitis</15>      Current Outpatient Medications   Medication Instructions    <16>baclofen</16> 5 mg, Oral, 2 Times Daily PRN, TAKE 1 TO 2 TABLETS BY MOUTH TWICE DAILY AS NEEDED FOR <17>HICCUPS</17>    <18>calcium carbonate/vitamin D3</18> (<19>VITAMIN D-3 ORAL</19>) Oral    <20>lidocaine-prilocaine</20> (<21>EMLA</21>) 2.5-2.5 % cream Apply cream one hour before <22>port access</22> as needed for <23>pain</23>.    <24>loperamide</24> (<25>IMODIUM</25>) 2 mg capsule Take two capsules by mouth at the onset of <26>diarrhea</26>, then take one capsule every 2 hours until <27>diarrhea-free</27> for 12 hours.    <28>LORazepam</28> (<29>ATIVAN</29>) 1 mg, Oral, Every 6 Hours PRN    <30>ondansetron</30> (<31>ZOFRAN</31>) 8 mg tablet Take 1 tablet three times a day as needed for <32>nausea</32> and <33>vomiting</33>. Start 2 days after last dose of <34>palonosetron</34> (*****) is given.    <35>prochlorperazine</35> (<36>COMPAZINE</36>) 10 mg, Oral, Every 6 Hours PRN    <37>selenium</37> 200 mcg tablet Oral, Daily Scheduled
