ner_results: ```plaintext
 with (+) metastatic <1>adenocarcinoma</1> in his ascitic fluid (<2>paracentesis</2> 06/07/2020).    He initiated <3>chemotherapy</3> with ***** on 03/20/2020 and received a total of 6 cycles through 06/05/2020, requiring dose reductions (<4>irinotecan</4> 90 mg/m2, <5>oxaliplatin</5> 68 mg/m2) by the end. His disease course has been notable for recurrent <6>large bowel obstruction</6>, initially treated with <7>colonic stent placement</7> back in April; then, with recurrent symptoms last month, requiring a prolonged <8>hospital admission</8> at ***** campus from June 14 - 07/19/2020. He was managed symptomatically with <9>NGT decompression</9>, <10>octreotide</10>, <11>dexamethasone</11>, and <12>pain management</12>, with the obstruction gradually resolving. He was also rx'ed for an <13>MSSA bacteremia</13> with a 4-week course of <14>IV antibiotics</14>. We had a <15>GOC discussion</15> while he was in the hospital, at which time he expressed a desire to remain proactive with further rx if at all possible.    Review of systems  Since discharge from the hospital, Mr. ***** reports:  - Home <16>VNA services</16> once weekly, plus sister is now living with him at his home. Patient himself does require fairly regular assistance with most <17>ADLs</17> and with <18>ambulation</18>.  - <19>Pain management</19> consists of <20>Fentanyl patch</20> plus <21>Dilaudid</21> for breakthrough; fair control (better at night than during the daytime).  - Tolerating some solid <22>POs</22>, with occasional postprandial <23>nausea/vomiting</23>.  - (+) passing <24>flatus</24> and <25>semi-solid BMs</25>  - No recent <26>fevers</26>
``` 
