 time (<1>CT scans</1> 04/08/2020) showed further <2>disease progression</2> in <3>lungs</3>, <4>liver</4>, and <5>lymph nodes</5>. <6>Liver biopsy</6> the following day confirmed <7>adenocarcinoma</7>    After extensive discussions w/Ms. ***** and her family re: her prognosis and the role and potential toxicities a/w <8>systemic therapy</8> esp in light of her challenging social circumstances (including ongoing heavy <9>EtOH consumption</9>), she ultimately initiated <10>chemotherapy</10> with empirically dose-reduced ***** beginning on 05/26/2020. Repeat <11>CT scans</11> after 4 treatment cycles showed reasonable <12>disease control</12> with only one area of slight growth in the <13>liver</13> (segment 8), but other areas (<14>liver</14>, <15>lung</15>, <16>LNs</16>) stable or slightly decreased in size; furthermore, she appeared to be deriving ***** favorable clinical benefit from treatment. On these bases, she continued with the same ***** regimen, with repeat <17>CT scans</17> after 8 cycles showing, again, only slight increase in ***** single <18>hepatic lesion</18>, this time in segment 2. She has since gone on to complete 11 cycles of <19>chemotherapy</19> in total, most recently on 10/21/2020.    Interval history/review of systems  - Some cumulative treatment-related <20>fatigue</20>  - <21>Abdominal pain</21> fairly well-controlled on stable dose of ***** *****  - <22>Sluggish appetite</22>  - Fairly regular <23>BMs</23>  - Mild non-progressive, non-debilitating <24>peripheral sensory neuropathy</24>  - Splits time between living independently at home and with family  - No <25>SOB</25>, <26>cough</26>, or <27>respiratory symptoms</27>.  - Family indicates she is still smoking and drinking <28>EtOH</28> ***** fair amount each day.      Current Outpatient Medications   Medication Instructions    <29>acetaminophen (TYLENOL)</29> 1,000 mg, Oral, Every 8 Hours Scheduled    <30>albuterol</30> 90 mcg/actuation metered dose inhaler 2 puffs, Inhalation, Every 6