be biopsied via <1>EBUS</1> if clinically indicated.     06/05/19: <2>Biopsy</2> of <3>hypermetabolic nodule</3> medial to <4>right lung</4> which came back consistent with <5>adenocarcinoma with mucinous differentiation</5>.    06/06/20: 3rd <6>EUS</6> showed ***** defined <7>16.8x12.7mm hypoechoic mass</7> in the neck of the <8>pancreas</8>, causing <9>mild upstream pancreatic duct dilation</9> to <10>5.4mm</10>. The mass abuts the <11>GDA</11> and <12>SMV</12> at the <13>portal confluence</13>. No clear abutment of <14>SMA</14> appreciated, although <15>SMA abutment</15> noted on <16>CT</16>. An <17>FNA</17> confirmed an <18>adenocarcinoma</18>.    06/25/20: Consultation with Dr. ***** who recommended definitive therapy with <19>chemotherapy</19>.    06/26/20: ***** with Dr. ***** and consented to *****#*****, Precision ***** trial. Patient was later found to not be eligible and so was recommended to start <20>SOC</20> *****.    07/20/20: <21>C1D1</21> *****. <22>CA 19-9</22> = <23>105</23>  08/02/20: ***** ***** - <24>Irinotecan</24> dose reduced by <25>20%</25> d/t <26>diarrhea</26> and <27>fatigue</27>    08/16/20: Cycle 3 was held due to ongoing <28>diarrhea</28>.     <29>Infectious causes</29> for <30>diarrhea</30> were ruled out, tested negative for *****. <31>UDP</31> ***** <32>1A test</32> result found that he is at <33>low risk of irinotecan toxicity</33>. <34>Genotype</34> : *****1/*****1 (Homozygous October 29 ***** repeats). Interpretation: <35>Low risk of irinotecan toxicity</35>. The overall risk of toxicity in patients heterozygous or homozygous for the <36>7 repeats</36> (*****1/*****28 or *****28/*****28) is approximately <37>13%</37> and <38>50%</38>, Respectively. He tried and failed <39>lomotil</39> and <40>imodium</40>, and was then started on <41>Octreotide 100 mcg/mL SQ TID</41> which did help control <42>diarrhea</42>.
