 CTCAE grade <1>3</1> <2>ANC</2> of <3>0.97</3>. <4>Gemcitabine</4> was resumed <5>1 week</5> later with a <6>20%</6> dose reduction (<7>800 mg/m2</7>). Her third infusion was held again last week for another episode of grade <8>3</8> <9>neutropenia</9> (<10>0.75</10>). The patient tolerated her first <11>2 infusions</11> of <12>gemcitabine</12> well with no <13>nausea</13>, change in <14>bowel habits</14>, <15>rash</15> or <16>fatigue</16>. <17>Low back pain</17> increased following initiation of therapy, which prompted repeat imaging that demonstrated <18>disease recurrence</18> in the <19>mesentery</19>. Given non-response to <20>gemcitabine</20>, her treatment was changed to a <21>5-*****-based regimen</21>. She tolerated a first cycle of <22>5-***** plus oxaliplatin</22> on <23>November 28</23>, without difficulty. Her regimen was escalated to <24>*****</24> with cycle <25>2</25> on <26>December 12</26>. She subsequently developed <27>alopecia</27>, <28>intractable nausea/vomiting</28>, and <29>diarrhea</29> requiring <30>hospitalization</30> for symptom control and multiple visits to the <31>Infusion Center</31> for <32>rehydration</32> and <33>potassium repletion</33> over a period of a <34>month</34>. In light of the severity of her toxicity profile following a single dose of <35>irinotecan</35>, testing for <36>UGT1A1 polymorphism</36> was performed which returned as <37>*****1/*****1</37>. She resumed <38>*****</38> (dosed with <39>25%</39> dose-reduction of <40>oxaliplatin</40> and omission of <41>5-***** bolus</41>) on <42>February 01</42>. Restaging scans after <43>8 total cycles</43> of dose-reduced <44>*****</44> demonstrated no measurable <45>*****</45>. Her <46>*****-9</46> decreased from <47>>3500</47> to <48>78</48> while on <49>*****</49>. She <50>*****</50> on a treatment holiday in <51>April</51>; however, her <52>*****-9</52> <53>*****</53> up and restaging scans in <54>mid-May</54> demonstrated <55>2 new 1.2 cm lesions</55> in the <56>liver</56> and <57>Gerota's fascia</57>. She resumed <58>chemotherapy</58> with <59>5-***** alone</59>, with a <60>*****-9</60> that increased from <61>1682</61> to <62>>8000</62>. Ms. ***** subsequently completed <63>two additional cycles</63> of <64>*****</64>, with a <65>*****-9</65> that continued to rise. Restaging imaging demonstrated <66>disease progression</66> with more prominent <67>soft tissue infiltration</67> inferior to the <68>pancreatectomy bed</68>, interval increase in size of <69>soft tissue masses</69> along the inferior <70>liver</70> and along right <71>Gerota's fascia</71>, and a new <72>intrahepatic lesion</72> in <73>hepatic segment 2</73>, compatible with new <74>metastasis</74>. Imaging also revealed significant <75>gastric distention</75>; however, a <76>barium swallow study</76> showed no evidence of <77>gastric outlet obstruction</77>.
