ner_results: ```plaintext
 review, the immunophenotype in  the current biopsy is compatible with <1>pancreatic origin</1>.The  absence of <2>TTF-1 expression</2> provides no support for a primary <3>lung adenocarcinoma</3>. Clinical and radiological correlation is  recommended.    Imaging  <4>CT CAP</4> 11/14/15  1. Postsurgical changes of <5>distal pancreatectomy</5> and <6>splenectomy</6>.   Unchanged soft tissue at the postsurgical site extending posteriorly   to surround the <7>superior mesenteric artery</7>, likely postsurgical.     2. Similar to decreased size of likely metastatic <8>mesenteric lymph nodes</8>.    3. Similar <9>cavernous transformation of the main portal vein</9> with   associated <10>varices</10>.    4. Evolving <11>postradiation changes</11> in the <12>left lung</12>. Nonspecific new   0.3 cm <13>pulmonary nodule</13> in the <14>lingula</14>. Attention on follow-up.     ASSESSMENT & PLAN  In summary, ***** ***** ***** ***** is a 67 y.o. male who presents to our <15>GI Oncology practice</15> at the <16>UCSF ***** ***** Family Comprehensive Cancer Center</16> for evaluation of <17>metastatic pancreatic adenocarcinoma</17>. Patient received 4 cycles of ***** in the <18>neoadjuvant setting</18> and then <19>gemcitabine</19> in the <20>adjuvant setting</20> for 6 months (completed in December 2012). He then had recurrence in the <21>lungs</21> in 2014 for which he had *****. Most recently, he has been getting therapy with <22>gemcitabine monotherapy</22> (<23>Abraxane</23> d/c'ed in July 2015 due to <24>neuropathy</24>) and has <25>stable disease</25> on the most recent <26>restaging scans</26> obtained on 11/14/15. His <27>CA 19-9</27> also has been declining since starting <28>gemcitabine</28> and *****-<29>paclitaxel</29> in April 2015.    At this point, he continues to be on <30>gemcitabine monotherapy</30>. I agree with omission of *****-<31>paclitaxel</31> due to the <32>grade 2 neuropathy</32>. <33>Restaging scans</33> can be obtained after 2 months of therapy (at the end of December and early January 2016) along with monthly <34>CA 19-9 levels</34> to monitor treatment response. If there is <35>disease progression</35> at that time, he can be considered for potential <36>trials</36> or he may be considered for <37>5FU</37>.
``` 
