combined with <1>liposomal irinotecan</1> (*****-*****). In the phase III *****-1 trial, <2>irinotecan liposome injection</2> in combination with <3>5-fluorouracil</3> (5-*****) and <4>leucovorin</4> demonstrated a 1.9-month improvement in <5>overall survival</5> (OS) with the addition of <6>irinotecan liposome injection</6> to <7>5-fluorouracil</7> (***** et al. J Clin *****. ***** ***** 2015). <8>Irinotecan liposome injection</8> dosing is at 70 mg/m2 + <9>5-fluorouracil</9> at 2400 mg/m2 over 46-48 hours every 2 weeks. The most commonly reported grade ?3 <10>adverse events</10> (AEs) with the combination were <11>neutropenia</11> (20%), <12>fatigue</12> (14%), <13>diarrhea</13> (13%), <14>vomiting</14> (11%), <15>nausea</15> (8%), <16>asthenia</16> (8%), and <17>abdominal pain</17> (7%). If he continues to have <18>stable disease</18> with only a few <19>mesenteric nodule involvement</19> for some period of time, <20>surgical resection</20> of these nodules may be considered (though it is not common practice). Patient understands that even if this was a possibility, it would unlikely be a curative approach but would be indicated due to his young age, indolent disease and could be considered as an opportunity to turn back the clock. In addition, in light of the recent data regarding the potential role of <21>immunotherapy</21> in *****-H <22>metastatic pancreatic cancers</22>, I would recommend obtaining <23>MMR</23> via <24>IHC</24> or <25>MSI status</25> via <26>PCR</26> (Le D, et al. ***** 2016 Annual Meeting; ***** 195). #Supportive care: He will continue with ***** with meals. He will continue to use <27>gabapentin</27> for his <28>neuropathy</28>. I encouraged him to maintain his weight and to remain active while undergoing therapy. We provided the patient with information regarding our clinic hours, phone number, important details of precautions during therapy. I provided them with an opportunity to ask questions and I believe that all of their questions have been answered to their satisfaction. We encouraged him to contact us with any questions or concerns. I would be happy to see the patient back in my clinic at any point in the future. Thank you for
``` 
