ner_results: ```plaintext
possibility of <1>neoplastic involvement</1> of the <2>duodenum</2> is considered. Lower abdominal mesenteric irregular spiculated <3>mass</3> adjacent to the <4>sigmoid colon</4> measuring 1.2 x 1 x 2.2 cm is nonspecific but concerning for a <5>neoplastic process</5>. <6>CT Chest W Contrast</6>: Small bilateral <7>pleural effusions</7> with associated lower lobe <8>atelectasis</8>. Abnormal mural thickening involving the distal <9>esophagus</9>, correlate clinically recommend correlation with recent <10>endoscopy</10>. Distended <11>stomach</11>.

01/06/18: <12>EGD</12>: <13>ESOPHAGUS</13> - <14>Erosive esophagitis</14>: Grade D -- mucosal breaks extending between folds involving >75% of circumference. <15>STOMACH</15> - High grade <16>pyloric stenosis</16>. Abundant fluid in <17>stomach</17> that was suctioned out completely. The <18>endoscope</18> could not be advanced through the strictured <19>pylorus</19>. <20>Balloon dilation</20> was then done by advancing a <21>wire</21> through the <22>pylorus</22> into the <23>duodenum</23> and then serial dilation from 8 mm to 10 mm. The <24>endoscope</24> could then be advanced into the <25>duodenum</25>. <26>DUODENUM</26> - ulcerated <27>duodenal bulb</27> as previously noted. <28>EUS</28>: Large hypoechoic amorphic <29>mass</29> in the <30>pancreatic head</30> measuring 43 mm x 39 mm. The <31>mass</31> obstructed the main <32>pancreatic duct</32> which was dilated to 11 mm. The <33>mass</33> also infiltrated into the <34>duodenal bulb</34> and there was compression and apparent involvement of the <35>splenic vein</35>/<36>portal vein confluence</36>. It was difficult to determine the extent of involvement of the <37>vessel</37>, and there was flow within the <38>vessel</38>. No obvious <39>mass</39> seen extending into the <40>vessel</40>.

01/08/18: Underwent <41>palliative surgery</41> for <42>gastric outlet obstruction</42>. S/p <43>gastrojejunostomy</43>, <44>cholecystojejunostomy</44>, <45>exploratory laparotomy</45> and <46>biopsy</46> of <47>mesenteric nodules</47> x 3. <48>Pathology</48> from <49>peritoneal/mesentery biopsies</49>: <50>adenocarcinoma</50> c/w <51>upper GI primary</51>. C/b Right arm <52>superficial thrombophlebitis</52> involving both the <53>basilic vein</53> and <54>cephalic veins</54>, no e/o <55>DVT</55>.

03/18/18: <56>PET/CT</56> 1. Ill-defined <57>FDG avid mass</57> predominantly centered at the <58>duodenum</58> adjacent.
``` 
