<1>bile duct</1>, <2>common hepatic</2>, and <3>intrahepatic ducts</3>. With <4>guidewire</4> in the <5>bile duct</5>, a small <6>biliary sphincterotomy</6> was performed using the <7>sphincterotome</7>. A covered metal <8>10 mm by 6 cm stent</8> was then deployed. ***** and <9>contrast</9> ***** freely. <10>EUS</10>: Bulging <11>ampulla</11> without any mucosal evidence of <12>tumor</12>. Endosonographic views showed a <13>submucosal ampullary lesion</13> extending into the <14>distal common bile duct</14>. <15>FNA</15> = at least high grade dysplasia within a <16>papillary neoplasm</16>.  - 03/21/20: <17>CA 19-9</17>: <18>153</18>  - 03/18/20: ***** with Dr. ***** ***** of our <19>Surgical faculty practice</19> and team for <20>surgical evaluation</20>; ***** <21>pancreaticoduodenectomy</21> for an <22>ampullary mass</22> that shows <23>high grade dysplasia</23> and is not amenable to <24>endoscopic excision</24>.  - 04/03/20: <25>Germline genetic testing</25> (Invitae <26>87-***** panel</26>): No pathogenic variants. <27>VUS x2</27>: <28>ALK (c.886G>C)</28>, ***** <29>c.490C>G</29>.  - 05/14/20: Underwent <30>pylorus-preserving *****</30> with Drs. ***** and *****. <31>Pathology</31> showed <32>pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma</32>, <33>2.1 cm</33>, invading <34>duodenal submucosa</34>, negative margins, and separate <35>intra-ampullary papillary-tubular neoplasm</35> (*****) with <36>high-grade dysplasia</36>, <37>2 cm</37>, negative margins. No <38>tumor</38> in <39>37 lymph nodes</39> (0/37). Final <40>TNM stage</40> for the <41>pancreas adenocarcinoma</41> = <42>pT2N0</42>.  - 05/23/20: Discharged post-operatively.  - *****/*****/*****-*****/*****/*****: Readmitted for <43>leukocytosis</43> and <44>purulent drain output</44> c/f <45>intra-abdominal infection</45>. Discharged with additional 14 days of <46>cipro</46>/<47>flagyl</47>. ***** removed by *****. *****.  - 06/05/2020: Seen by me in ***** ***** <48>Onc</48>; discussed possible role for <49>adjuvant chemotherapy</49> after further recovery from <50>surgery</50> and above-noted <51>postoperative complications</51>.  - 07/22/2020: Recovered adequately to begin <52>chemotherapy</52> with single-agent <53>gemcitabine</53> ***** three-week-on, one-week-off dosing schedule. - 09/30/2020: Interval <54>re-imaging</54>: Increased size of multiple scattered <55>pulmonary nodules</55>, up to <56>1 cm</56> in size, suspicious for <57>metastatic disease</57>; no change in
``` 
