ner_results: ```plaintext
 and lower lobes which has increased in size compared to 06/01/2019. For example, the <1>mass</1> in the <2>right middle lobe</2> at the level of the <3>cavoatrial junction</3> measures approximately <4>5.0 x 10.0 cm</4> in maximal transverse dimensions (previously <5>8.1 x 4.2 cm</5>). Similar to prior, the <6>mass</6> invades the <7>anterior chest wall</7> and <8>mediastinum</8> where it abuts the <9>right heart border</9> with loss of intervening fat plane between the <10>mass</10> and <11>right atrial blood pool</11>. The <12>mass</12> also extends to the <13>right hilum</13> where it encases but does not significantly narrow the <14>pulmonary artery</14> and <15>vein branches</15>. Increased <16>groundglass opacity</16> and <17>interlobular septal thickening</17> throughout the aerated <18>right middle</18> and <19>lower lobes</19>, compatible with worsening <20>lymphangitic spread of tumor</20>.    Increased <21>groundglass opacity</21> and <22>interlobular septal thickening</22> in the <23>left lower lobe</23> at the site of treated <24>metastasis</24> which may represent posttreatment change. Remaining <25>pulmonary nodules</25> in the <26>left lung</26> are not significantly changed.    <27>PLEURA</27>:  No <28>pleural effusion</28>. Redemonstration of diffuse <29>right pleural nodularity</29> and enhancement compatible with <30>pleural metastases</30>.    <31>MEDIASTINUM</31>:   Similar appearance of <32>right hilar lymphadenopathy</32>.    <33>HEART</33>/***** *****:  Normal <34>heart size</34>. No <35>pericardial effusion</35>. Normal caliber of the <36>aortic root</36> and <37>pulmonary artery</37>.    <38>BONES</38>/<39>SOFT TISSUES</39>:  Increased conspicuity of <40>sclerotic lesions</40> involving multiple <41>ribs</41>, <42>right greater than left</42>, and the <43>right inferior sternal body</43>, compatible with <44>osseous metastases</44>.    <45>IMPRESSION</45>:   1.  Worsening <46>metastatic disease</46> in the <47>right middle</47> and <48>lower lobes</48> with increased <49>tumor-related consolidation</49> and <50>lymphangitic spread of tumor</50>.    2.  Increased <51>ground glass opacity</51> in the <52>left lower lobe</52> at site of prior <53>radiation</53> which may reflect evolving posttreatment change, however progression of <54>tumor</54> is not excluded. ***** of <55>metastatic disease</55> in the <56>left lung</56> is otherwise unchanged.    3.  
