ner_results: ```plaintext
 radiology reports, as follows:     03/21/2021 <1>CT ABDOMEN/PELVIS</1>  FINDINGS:  Lower thorax: <2>Right atrial enlargement</2>.     Liver and biliary tree: <3>Biliary stent</3> from the right hepatic duct into the duodenum. Interval placement of biliary stent with tip in the left hepatic duct with tip in the proximal jejunum. Similar degree of <4>intrahepatic bile ductal dilation</4>, left greater than right. Interval increase in biliary enhancement (for example August 64). Multiple wedge-shaped peripheral areas of <5>hypoattenuation</5>, predominantly of the right hepatic lobe, which are increased/new from prior, the largest in segment 4A/8 (November 42 and August 46). These regions do not persist on delayed imaging however there is some new faint capsular retraction. Some of these areas have small associated lesions which are new, for example the 5 mm lesions in segment October 02 (July 38-40 and 03/12/16). Unchanged <6>hepatic cysts</6>.     Gallbladder: <7>Fundal adenomyomatosis</7>.     Spleen: <8>Punctate calcified granulomas</8>.     Pancreas: Similar <9>atrophy of the pancreatic body and tail</9>. Main pancreatic duct is similarly dilated measuring up to 9 mm with focal tapering at the head the level of the ***** <10>pancreatic mass</10> measuring approximately 2.0 x 2.0 cm (August 98), previously measuring 2.1 x 1.9 cm. The splenic and portal vein are encased by <11>tumor</11>. This mass causes mild <12>portal vein stenosis</12> and moderate to severe <13>splenic vein stenosis</13> (September 070). The splenic artery and proper hepatic artery are encased by tumor with severe stenosis of the proper hepatic (August 92) and moderate narrowing of the splenic artery (July 93). Similar stranding around the <14>SMA</14> and <15>celiac root</15>.     Adrenal glands: Unchanged nodular thickening of the left adrenal gland. The right adrenal gland is normal.     Kidneys and ureters: Subcentimeter <16>renal hypodensities</16> are too small to characterize but are statistically likely to represent <17>renal cysts</17>. <18>Punctate hyperattenuating focus</18> of the right interpolar region,
``` 
