 the goals of such treatment treatment are to produce disease control and hopefully extend survival, while possibly alleviating <1>cancer-related symptoms</1>, but would not be expected to achieve cure.    There are several possible <2>chemotherapy</2> options for <3>metastatic pancreatic cancer</3>, with the choice of therapy depending on the patient's age, performance status, co-morbid conditions, and personal preference. The two current gold standards for front-line treatment, based on phase III data, include:    - ***** (biweekly ***** <4>5-*****</4>, <5>leucovorin</5>, <6>irinotecan</6>, and <7>oxaliplatin</7>), which was shown in a phase III French cooperative group trial to be superior to <8>gemcitabine monotherapy</8> for patients with <9>metastatic pancreatic cancer</9> in terms of overall survival, <10>PFS</10>, *****, and other clinical outcomes. Side effects of this regimen were discussed, including but not limited to <11>immunosuppression</11>, <12>risk of infection</12>, <13>hair loss</13>, <14>fatigue</14>, <15>nausea</15>, <16>vomiting</16>, <17>diarrhea</17>, and <18>peripheral sensory neuropathy</18>. I explained that this regimen requires placement of a <19>Mediport</19> due to the ***** component of therapy (48 hour infusion of <20>5-*****</20>). Furthermore, because of the high incidence of grade _ <21>neutropenia</21> with this regimen, we tend to give primary prophylaxis with <22>growth factor support</22> (***** or <23>Neupogen</23>) after each treatment cycle.  - The combination of <24>gemcitabine</24> plus *****-<25>paclitaxel</25>, which was shown in a phase III international trial (*****) also to be superior to <26>gemcitabine monotherapy</26> for patients with <27>metastatic pancreatic cancer</27>. Side effects and logistics of this regimen were also explained.  - For patients too frail or with medical co-morbidities that may preclude the administration of combination <28>chemotherapy</28>, <29>gemcitabine monotherapy</29> represents an appropriate choice.    Certainly <30>clinical trials</30> also represent an ideal option. We discussed with the patient in detail about two study possibilities we have available here at ***** for 
