 the first-line treatment of <1>metastatic pancreatic cancer</1>, and he was sent consent forms for both of these ahead of time to review:  (1) the ***** trial, a randomized phase II trial evaluating the combination of <2>gemcitabine</2> plus <3>*****-paclitaxel</3> with or without *****-*****, a bispecific monoclonal antibody directed against <4>IGF-1R</4> and *****. For this study, patients are initially screened by measurement of <5>serum free IGF-1 levels</5>, as only those with high <6>IGF-1 levels</6> are randomized. The study also requires <7>tumor tissue</7> for assessment of intratumoral <8>Heregulin (HRG) expression</8>, although there is no cutoff for study eligibility. ***** the nature of <9>clinical trial</9> and specifically the study rationale, treatment regimen, <10>screening tests</10> and logistics of the above <11>clinical trial</11>.   (2) a phase II trial consisting of the combination of <12>gemcitabine</12>/<13>*****-paclitaxel</13> plus <14>ibrutinib</14>.    After much discussion and consideration, the patient is inclined to move ahead with <15>SOC chemotherapy</15> with *****. He is in fact already scheduled to have a <16>Mediport</16> placed through his local oncologist tomorrow, and will let us know w/i the next day or so whether he wishes to receive his treatment locally vs here at *****.    The other issues we covered included:  - <17>Pain management</17>: A new script for ***** ***** was provided for <18>long-acting RTC pain control</18>. Future consideration could be made for <19>EUS-guided celiac plexus nerve block</19> as well if he does not respond adequate to <20>opioid analgesics</20>.  - Given his young age at presentation, I will make a referral for him to be seen at our <21>Cancer Risk program</21> for <22>genetic counseling</22>, despite the absence of a family history of cancer.  - The patient does have some pain referrable to the <23>sacrum</23>, with <24>PET</24> and <25>MRI</25> suggesting some <26>osseous metastases</26> in that area. For now, I will see how this responds to <27>systemic therapy</27>, but we could consider <28>spot RT</28> to that area in the future.    All of the patient's questions 
 were answered to his and his partner's satisfaction. If he chooses to receive his care at ***** we will get him set up to start within the next week or so.  
``` 
