<1>Carcinoembryonic Antigen</1> 381.7 (H) 08/16/2019    <2>Carcinoembryonic Antigen</2> 376.1 (H) 07/18/2019     PATHOLOGY  Source of Specimen:  <3>Liver</3>, <4>computed tomography-guided fine needle aspiration biopsy</4>      FINAL CYTOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:  *****. *****, *****-guided fine needle aspiration biopsy:    Rare atypical epithelial cells, suspicious for <5>adenocarcinoma</5>. See comment.    COMMENTS:   The ***** are moderately cellular and reveal rare atypical glandular cells in a background of benign <6>hepatocytes</6>. The atypical cells are seen  to best advantage on the cell block. The atypical cells are mildly enlarged with dense vacuolated cytoplasm and have enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with irregular contours and coarse chromatin.  <7>Immunohistochemical</7> and <8>cytochemical stains</8> were performed on block A1 with the following results in atypical cells:    Stain      Target      Result  <9>CK7</9>      Epithelial      Positive  <10>MOC-31</10>      Epithelial      Positive  *****     <11>Hepatocytes</11>     Negative (+in hepatocytes)  *****      <12>Mucin</12>      Positive    The staining pattern supports the morphologic findings. Overall, the findings are atypical and suspicious for <13>adenocarcinoma</13>; however the  paucity of tumor cells present precludes definitive diagnosis.    Imaging  <14>Ct Abdomen /pelvis With Contrast</14>    Result Date: 09/18/2019  <15>CT ABDOMEN/PELVIS WITH CONTRAST</15>  *****/*****/***** 11:51 AM CLINICAL HISTORY: 58-year-old female presenting with <16>stage IV pancreatic cancer</16>, on <17>chemotherapy</17>, evaluation for disease progression. COMPARISON:  Multiple exams with the most recent study 08/01/2019 TECHNIQUE: Following the administration of 150 cc of <18>Omnipaque 350</18>, contiguous 1.25-mm collimation axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis. Coronal and sagittal reformats were also obtained. FINDINGS: Visualized lung bases:  Unremarkable <19>Liver</19>: Similar in size and number of multiple <20>hepatic metastasis</20> accounting for difference in respiratory phase and liver position.
