female who presents to our GI Oncology practice at the UCSF ***** ***** Family Comprehensive Cancer Center for a follow-up visit of metastatic <1>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</1> with biopsy proven <2>liver metastasis</2>. Patient was started on ***** <3>06/07/19</3> and has been tolerating it well with dose reduction of <4>irinotecan</4> by 20% starting with <5>cycle 2</5>. Her restaging scans from <6>08/01/2019</6> showed increase in the size of the <7>hepatic lesions</7>. However, the scans were compared to <8>05/17/19</8> which was prior to the start of <9>chemotherapy</9> on <10>06/07/19</10>. For this reason, we recommended to continue on ***** as we were not certain if this is true progression due to the lag time between the comparator scan and the current scan. She continued to have clinical decline with worsening <11>fatigue</11> and also <12>weight loss</12>. She requested a week delay in <13>chemotherapy</13> which has helped with her symptoms. She has now completed <14>7 cycles of chemotherapy</14>. Her most recent restaging scans from <15>09/18/19</15> showed overall stable disease in the liver but increase in the size of the <16>pancreatic primary</16>. I called and spoke with the radiologist to get a better understanding of the primary <17>pancreatic tumor</17> characterization. He noted that there is increased enhancement around the tumor so concerning for progressive disease. As her ***** has not decreased either and she has had a difficult time tolerating this regimen, my recommendation is to switch her therapy to <18>gemcitabine</18> combined with *****-<19>paclitaxel</19>. I reviewed the potential side effects of this regimen including but not limited to: <20>neuropathy</20>, <21>cytopenias</21> increasing the risk of <22>infections</22> and <23>bleeding</23>, requirements for <24>blood transfusions</24>, <25>alopecia</25>, <26>rash</26>, <27>edema</27>, <28>fatigue</28>, <29>infusion reaction</29>, <30>nausea/vomiting</30>, <31>myalgias</31>. She will also undergo formal <32>chemo teach</32> prior to starting. -plan for <33>gemcitabine 1000 mg/m2</33> + *****-<34>paclitaxel 125 mg/m2</34> on days 1, 8, 15 out of <35>28-day cycle</35>. -We will plan for a <36>CT chest</36>,
``` 
