03/05/20: Restarted treatment ***** *****  03/19/20: ***** *****  *****/*****/*****-*****/*****/*****: Hospitalized with <1>abdominal pain</1> and found to have <2>gallbladder fossa abscess</2> and <3>Klebsiella bacteremia</3> s/p <4>percutaneous drain placement</4> 03/28/20.  Also received <5>Zosyn</5>, transitioned to <6>Augmentin</6> to complete total <7>14d course</7> on 04/10/20.  04/25/20: <8>Percutaneous drain</8> was removed by *****  05/02/20: C4D1 *****  05/19/20: ***** *****  06/04/20: <9>CT CAP</9>: <10>stable disease</10>, resolved <11>abdominal fluid collection</11>  06/06/20: ***** *****  06/20/20: ***** *****. Patient experienced <12>grade 2 reaction</12> during <13>oxaliplatin infusion</13>. <14>Benadryl 25mg IV</14> was administered, and the patient reported near immediate relief. Patient tolerated the infusion re-challenge up to ***** rate. He completed the <15>oxaliplatin</15> without further incident. <16>CA 19-9</16> = <17>136</17>  07/04/20: ***** ***** ***** <18>19-9=93</18>  07/16/20: <19>CT CAP pancreatic protocol</19>: <20>Stable disease</20>.   08/12/20: ***** with <21>PV resection</21>. Post op course c/b prolonged hospital stay due to <22>ileus</22> and <23>delayed gastric emptying</23>, <24>aspiration pneumonia</24>, and <25>pancreatic leak</25>. Post op <26>ileus</26> and ***** required prolonged <27>bowel rest</27>, <28>parenteral nutrition</28>, and <29>NG placement</29> multiple times. <30>Reglan</30> was added to his medications and his diet was slowly advanced to a <31>minced diet</31> with <32>nectar thick</32> ***** September 01. He also developed <33>aspiration PNA</33> and was found to have <34>right vocal cord paralysis</34> during evaluation by <35>OHNS</35>.  Also c/b infected <36>pancreatic leak</36> s/p <37>IR drain</37> and required <38>IV antibiotics</38>.  Discharged 09/08/20 to ***** <39>SNF</39> with <40>drain</40>, <41>TPN</41> and <42>IV abx</42>   10/20/20: <43>Drain removal</43>
``` 
