ner_results: ```plaintext
Thank you for referring Ms. ***** ***** ***** to the UCSF Comprehensive Cancer Center for evaluation of her <1>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</1>. I saw ***** ***** ***** ***** ***** Oncology practice at the UCSF Comprehensive Cancer Center in ***** ***** *****. ***** *****. History of Present Illness Ms. ***** is a 69 y.o. female who initially presented with <2>jaundice</2> in August 2011, at which time an <3>ERCP</3> with placement of <4>biliary stent</4> was performed for what presumably was a <5>malignant biliary stricture</5>. This was complicated by some post-procedure <6>pancreatitis</6>. Repeat <7>ERCP</7> with <8>EUS</8> at ***** apparently confirmed a <9>mass in the head of the pancreas</9>, which was biopsied and revealed <10>adenocarcinoma</10> (original report N/A). She underwent a ***** procedure on 10/01/11 at Chinese Hospital, with pathology revealing <11>moderately differentiated adenocarcinoma</11> measuring at least <12>2 cm</12> with no <13>lymph node involvement</13> (0/21 lymph nodes). The <14>tumor</14> was noted to invade <15>muscularis propria of duodenum</15> extending into <16>bile duct margin</16>. The patient was started on adjuvant <17>gemcitabine</17> starting on 01/05/12, originally dosed as weekly for 3 weeks for the first cycle, followed thereafter by once a month dosing for 6 cycles under the care of Dr. ***** *****. <18>CT abdomen/pelvis</18> obtained on 08/31/12 revealed a <19>1.7cm cystic structure in the pancreatic body</19> and a <20>new 1.5 soft tissue density posterior to the proximal SMA with partial encasement</20>. In addition there was an <21>ill-defined sclerotic density within the L2 vertebral body</21>. Subsequent <22>PET/CT</22> was obtained which showed <23>dilatation of the pancreatic duct in the body and tail</23> with a <24>cystic area proximal to it</24>, suggesting possible <25>recurrence</25>. There was also increased <26>FDG activity in the L2 vertebral body (SUV 4.9)</26> which corresponded to the <27>sclerotic lesion</27> concerning for <28>metastasis</28>, as well as the <29>1.5x1.4 cm soft tissue nodular lesion in the left paraaortic region</29> also concerning for <30>metastatic lymphadenopathy</30>.
``` 
