ner_results: ```plaintext
 of intravascular <1>tumor growth</1>.   However, areas of the main <2>tumor mass</2> such as A11 show similar  architectural properties, with malignant cells arranged in dilated  channels and surrounding by fibrous stroma. A6 shows mucin within a  <3>lymph node</3>, raising the possibility of <4>lymph node spread</4>.   <5>Immunohistochemical</5>, <6>in situ hybridization</6>, or <7>histochemical stains</7> were  necessary to evaluate this case and establish the correct diagnosis.   The following stains were performed and evaluated at ***** on block A6:    - <8>CD31</8>: Highlights vascular endothelium, does not show intravascular  <9>tumor</9>. This focus is interpreted as <10>invasive tumor</10> in <11>peripancreatic soft tissue</11>.   - <12>Keratin</12>: ***** single <13>tumor cells</13> and small clusters of cells less  than 0.2 mm in greatest diameter in association with mucin in a <14>lymph node</14>. An additional <15>H&E recut</15> shows similar features. May represent  in-transit <16>isolated tumor cells</16>. This is an evolving area as far as  clinical significance.    <17>MMR proteins</17> all intact by <18>IHC</18>.  ---------------------------------------------  His <19>postoperative course</19> was notable for <20>fevers</20> of unclear etiology, <21>rx'ed empirically with IV antibiotics/anti-fungal rx</21>; a <22>Hgb</22> that ***** at <23>6.2</23> for which he received <24>2u PRBCs</24>; and <25>insulin ggt</25> transitioned to a <26>subcutaneous regimen</26> prior to discharge.     He did require <27>hospital re-admission</27> from January 16 - 01/19/2019 due to <28>abdominal pain</28>.***** during this ***** a widely patent <29>anastomosis</29>,some mild <30>inflammation</30> around the <31>anastamosis</31> with no <32>ulceration</32>, ***** <33>gastropathy</33>. <34>Biopsies</34> were ***** no <35>malignancy</35> identified. He ***** on *****, a <36>PPI</36>, and <37>triple therapy</37> for<38>H.pylori</38>(although <39>bx</39> results showed no organisms).     <40>CT scans</40> performed during admission showed ***** ***** new <41>2.3 cm hepatic metastasis</41> in segment 8, along with extensive <42>peritoneal stranding</42> and <43>nodularity</43> of indeterminate significance. 
