ner_results: ```plaintext
 However, at the time of attempted <1>biopsy</1> (03/10/2019), this <2>liver lesion</2> was no longer discernible, and <3>biopsy</3> of the area showed only <4>steatohepatitis</4> in a background of moderate <5>steatosis</5>. Subsequent <6>CT scans</6> in June 2019 showed interval evolution of the <7>liver lesion</7>, now ***** in appearance and c/w posttreatment change or interval partial <8>necrosis</8>; as well as some interval increased soft tissue in the <9>para-aortic region</9> and at the <10>celiac</10> and <11>SMA origins</11>. At the time, he was also noted to have persistent <12>transaminitis</12> of indeterminate etiology (?possibly c/w <13>steatohepatitis</13> from ***** ***** <14>chemotherapy</14>; prior <15>hepatitis B serologies</15> negative), although his <16>LFTs</16> have come down since then, with only a slightly elevated <17>AST</17>.    Interval history/review of systems  Working part-time (self-owned catering and restaurant pop-ups); still with some easy <18>fatiguability</18>  No abdominal or back pain  <19>Blood sugars</19> well-controlled on current <20>insulin regimen</20> (fasting in low 100s)  Good appetite, uses <21>enzyme supplements</21> regularly with meals  <22>BMs</22> vary in consistency, up to 5-6x/day  Minimal residual peripheral <23>sensory neuropathy</23> from prior <24>chemotherapy</24>      Medications:  <25>Lantus</25> + <26>humalog insulin</26>  *****      Allergies/Contraindications  <27>No Known Allergies</27>      Comprehensive past medical, family, and social history which was performed during a previous encounter was re-examined and reviewed with the patient. There is nothing new to add at today's visit. For details, please refer to my original consultation note in this chart.        <28>ECOG Performance Status: 1</28>    PHYSICAL EXAM via video observation:   Vitals: Not performed as today's visit was conducted via video  Constitutional: Normal appearance. No acute distress. Not ill-appearing. Not diaphoretic.  Head: Normocephalic, atraumatic. External ears normal. Nose normal.    Eyes: Extraocular movements intact. Conjunctivae normal. No eye discharge. No scleral icterus.  Neck: Normal 
``` 
