bloody <1>bm</1> (only after eating), decreased/minimal <2>PO intake</2>, <3>diarrhea</3> with every <4>PO intake</4> since receiving <5>chemotherapy</5>. She also reported <6>fatigue</6>. RN advised that pt take <7>Zofran</7> <8>ATC</8>, pick up <9>imodium</9> that had been prescribed, and to increase intake of food, and to report if <10>bloody diarrhea</10> worsened. 05/10/20: Reported continued <11>diarrhea</11>, improved <12>bleeding</12>. <13>Potassium</13> <14>2.8</14>, <15>Mg</15> <16><2</16>, <17>Cr</17> <18>1.35</18> and <19>ANC</19> <20>900</20>. Received <21>60 mEQ potassium</21> with <22>IVF</22>, <23>1g Mg</23> and improvement in <24>K</24> to <25>3.8</25>, <26>Cr</26> to <27>0.98</27>. She was sent an <28>Rx</28> for <29>20mEq PO potassium</29> as well. Advised to take <30>ATC loperamide</30> until no <31>diarrhea</31> ***** 05/17/20: <32>Infusion center</32> for <33>labs</33> notable for <34>K</34> <35>3.0</35>, <36>Mg</36> <37>1.3</37>, <38>Cr</38> <39>1.32</39>. <40>WBC</40> <41>35</41>. Received <42>60mEq IV KCL</42>, <43>1g Magnesium</43>, <44>1L NS</44>. <45>Diarrhea</45> had resolved, but still with <46>fatigue</46>, <47>loss of appetite</47> 05/24/20: ***** ***** held as pt still recovering--<48>diarrhea</48> had resolved, but she still had poor <49>PO intake</49>, <50>fatigue</50> and preferred to wait an additional week so that she could have support at home. 05/31/20: ***** ***** (had been delayed by 1 week for pt recovery per her preference) 06/14/20: <51>C3</51> ***** delayed per pt preference to have an extra week to recover. She experienced continued <52>fatigue</52>, <53>loss of appetite</53> <54>diarrhea</54> with <55>C2</55>.
