appears that the risk:benefit ratio of pursuing further <1>chemotherapy</1> is unfavorable and I would strongly recommend against this. Similarly, I do not see palliative <2>radiation</2> (including *****) as offering any benefit in this scenario. Her family may wish her to try some <3>acupuncture</3> and/or <4>Chinese herbs</4> which I think would be fine. Otherwise, we will refocus our goals on purely palliative/symptomatic measures with a referral to home <5>hospice</5>, given that her expected longevity is likely measurable in weeks at this point. For now, I will prescribe her low-dose <6>Decadron</6> as an appetite stimulant, and have her receive a liter of <7>IV fluids</7> at our infusion center today. I spent a total of 30 minutes face-to-face with the patient, of which greater than 50% was spent in counseling regarding her <8>cancer diagnosis</8>.
