ner_results: ```plaintext
Spleen: Unremarkable Pancreas: No significant change in the <1>hypoattenuating necrotic pancreatic mass</1> in the <2>pancreatic body</2> that measures approximately <3>4.0 x 3.2 cm</3> in transaxial dimension. The mass encases and obliterates the <4>proximal celiac artery</4> and partially encases the <5>superior mesenteric artery</5>. The mass partially encases and significantly narrows the <6>superior mesenteric vein</6> and there is complete occlusion of the <7>splenic vein</7>. The <8>main portal vein</8> is patent but significantly narrowed at the ***** confluence. There is a marked amount of <9>venous congestion</9> in the pelvis due to the significant superior mesenteric vein narrowing. There is <10>atrophy of the pancreatic tail</10>. The <11>common bile duct</11> is nondilated. No intrahepatic biliary ductal dilation. Adrenal Glands: Unremarkable Kidneys: <12>Left kidney superior pole simple cyst</12> measuring <13>1.7-cm</13>. GI Tract: Note is made of <14>antral wall thickening</14> which was seen on prior. Pelvis: Unremarkable Lymphadenopathy: Absent Ascites: Absent Bones: No suspicious lesions IMPRESSION: 1. No significant change in size of the pancreatic body and tail necrotic mass. The mass is resulting in severe narrowing of the superior mesenteric vein and obliteration of the splenic vein. The celiac axis is completely encased and obstructed in its proximal portion. //ALERT// 2. New ill-defined low attenuating lesion in segment 6 of the <15>liver</15> is concerning for <16>metastatic disease</16>. 3. There is circumferential <17>gastric antral wall thickening</17> which may be secondary to <18>gastritis</18>. Impression and Recommendations: In summary, Ms. ***** appears to be doing well with her current <19>chemotherapy regimen</19> consisting of an alternating-week schedule of <20>gemcitabine</20> plus <21>capecitabine</21> for her <22>advanced pancreatic cancer</22>. She maintains a good ***** overall and her *****-<23>9 biomarker</23> has been declining. I went over in careful detail the radiographic findings from her recent <24>CT</24> with one of our radiologists, and
``` 
