REASON FOR CONSULTATION: Interested in management options for metastatic <1>adenocarcinoma</1> REFERRING PHYSICIAN: Patient is self-referred HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS: This is a very pleasant 58-year-old African American from ***** *****. He presented with <2>left flank pain</2> in September of last year and was found at that time to have <3>bilateral adrenal adenomas</3>. During his workup, he was also noted to have an elevated <4>PSA</4> of <5>5.1</5>. Eventually a <6>biopsy</6> was done of the <7>prostate</7> and this revealed a <8>stage II, T2</8> *****., ***** score <9>7</9> lesion. A <10>prostatectomy</10> was recommended. At some point during this workup, was appreciated that he had a <11>mass</11> in the <12>body of the pancreas</12> measuring <13>6.5 x 2.5 x 2.4 cm</13>. No extrahepatic disease was identified. A <14>PET/CT</14> was also done on March 09 which showed some increase in the <15>left supraclavicular lymph nodes</15> as well as uptake in the <16>prostate</16> and in the <17>pancreas</17>. There was no evidence of intra-abdominal metastases. At ***** of the pancreas was done on March 03 which revealed an <18>adenocarcinoma</18>. A <19>diagnostic laparoscopy</19> was done on March 22. This showed <20>multiple metastases</20> along the <21>right diaphragmatic surface</21> and <22>biopsies</22> were consistent with <23>metastatic adenocarcinoma</23>. <24>Bone scan</24> showed changes consistent with <25>arthritic or degenerative changes</25> in the <26>sternoclavicular</26> and <27>acromioclavicular joints</27>. He was seen at ***** for medical oncology consultation. Treatment with either <28>gemcitabine monotherapy</28> or modified ***** was recommended. A <29>clinical trial</29> was also discussed. Symptomatically, he is doing well. Initial pain that he had in the left flank actually resolved shortly after its appearance. His weight is been stable. He has a good appetite. He has normal bowel movements. He is doing all of his usual activities. PAST MEDICAL HISTORY: See below MEDICAL ILLNESSES: He has had <30>diabetes</30> for <31>2 years</31> and became <32>insulin-dependent</32> a <33>year ago</33>. He's had <34>hypertension</34> since <35>1996</35>.
