invasive carcinoma identified.  4 lymph nodes were negative. Pt did well until April 2016, when he developed <1>recurrent abdominal pain</1>, for which a repeat <2>CT AP</2> was obtained locally and showed a <3>dilated remnant distal bile duct</3> within the <4>pancreatic head</4>. <5>ERCP/EUS</5> on May 1716 (at *****) showed <6>1.5cm mass</6> in the <7>remnant distal bile duct</7> with <8>high grade dysplasia</8> on <9>biopsy</9> (notably, the <10>pancreas</10> appeared normal). He was scheduled to have ***** in June 2016, but declined <11>surgery</11> in favor of <12>herbal/alternative therapies</12>. He was lost to follow up until November 2019 when he presented with <13>abdominal pain</13> and a <14>CT A/P</14> on 12/14/19 showed an <15>enlarging pancreatic head mass</15> (compared to April 2016) though the official report comments on a normal <16>pancreas</16>. An <17>ERCP/EUS</17> performed locally on 12/27/19 showed an <18>ampullary mass</18>--<19>brushings of the bile duct</19> showed <20>non small cell carcinoma</20> while a <21>biopsy of the ampulla</21> of ***** showed <22>invasive adenocarcinoma</22>. After consultation with Dr. *****, plan was made for a ***** <23>resection</23> on 01/18/20. However, intraoperatively he was found to have a <24>pancreatic head mass</24> with <25>tumor involvement of the proper hepatic artery and portal vein</25>. After consultation with Dr. ***** in the OR, the <26>mass</26> was felt to be <27>unresectable</27>, and the <28>surgery</28> was aborted--rather a ***** <29>end-side hepatojejunostomy</29> was performed. <30>Pathology</30> from <31>biopsy of the pancreas</31> confirmed <32>invasive adenocarcinoma</32>. There was also <33>invasive adenocarcinoma</33> in the <34>bile duct excision</34>. He established care with UCSF GI Med Onc on 03/02/20. 03/07/20: <35>Pancreatic Tumor</35> *****: Reviewed <36>scans</36>, <37>pathology</37>. See 03/02/20 initial consult note for full TB discussion. Overall no consensus about whether <38>ampullary</38>, <39>biliary</39>, or <40>pancreatic</40>. Suggestion to <41>trt</41> with *****/<42>cis</42>/<43>abraxane</43> if tolerated. 03/16/20: Follow up: pt opted for *****/<44>abraxane</44> to <45>trt</45> ***** given c/f <46>toxicity</46> with <47>three drug regimen</47> 03/23/20: <48>C1D1</48> <49>Gemcitabine/Abraxane</49>. <50>1u pRBC</50> for <51>hemoglobin</51>. <52>CA 19-9</52> = <53>28</53> 03/30/20: ***** <54>Gemcitabine/Abraxane</54> 04/06/20: Presented for ***** *****/<55>abraxane</55>. <56>ANC</56> <57>500</57>. <58>Trt</58> held and given ***** x2. Pt subsequently opted to delay <59>trt</59> to April 20 so that he could meet his new grandchild.
``` 
