ner_results: ```plaintext
Subjective:    This is a very pleasant 66-year-old woman who we first saw in early May 2012.  At that time, she was status post pylorus sparing <1>procedure</1> done on 05/04/2012.  Pathology showed a <2>2.5 cm well to moderately differentiated adenocarcinoma</2> with a <3>positive retroperitoneal margin</3> in <4>8 of 12 lymph nodes</4> were also positive.  She was started on adjuvant treatment with fixed dose rate <5>gemcitabine</5> plus <6>capecitabine</6>.  She has completed <7>six 28 day cycles</7>.    She does have known <8>adnexal cystic lesions</8> and is being followed by her gynecologist.  A repeat <9>pelvic ultrasound</9> done in 2918 showed no change. She saw Dr. ***** regarding this. His impression is that this is benign and can also be followed with surveillance.     She also has evidence for <10>aortic stenosis</10> on <11>scan</11>. She has been evaluated for this and there is no current indication for intervention.    In March 2014, she developed <12>severe abdominal pain</12> and was admitted to the hospital for <13>pancreatitis</13>. Attempts at <14>enteroscopy</14> were unsuccessful and her symptoms resolved. In February of this year she also had another episode of <15>acute pancreatitis</15>. This resolved without sequelae. A followup <16>EUS</16> was done on 05/10/2015. This was unremarkable and <17>FNA</17> revealed <18>acute pancreatitis</18>.    She developed a <19>R frozen shoulder</19> and had <20>cortisone injections</20> about 1 year ago. She also had a similar problem in the <21>left shoulder</21> and was treated with <22>physical therapy</22> and repeated <23>cortisone injections</23>.    She's been seeing an endocrinologist because of fluctuating <24>calcium</24> and <25>potassium levels</25>. She was found to be <26>hyperthyroid</26> and she is now being treated with <27>methimazole</27>.    Her husband died at the end of December 2016. This has been very difficult for her but she is coping better now.     In November 2017, she developed an increase in a <28>nodular consolidation</28> in her <29>right lung</29>. This was <30>PET avid</30>. She was referred for a <31>VATS wedge resection</31> and this revealed a <32>mucinous</32>
``` 
