Extraperitoneal soft tissues: Unremarkable Lines/drains/medical devices: As above RADIATION DOSE INDICATORS: ***** *****: <1>7</1> , <2>CTDIvol Min</2>: <3>4.4 mGy</3>, <4>CTDIvol Max</4>: <5>16.9 mGy</5>, <6>DLP</6>: <7>1065.2 mGy.cm</7>. The following accession numbers are related to this dose report *****,*****     1.  Compared to the prior <8>abdomen/pelvis CT</8> <9>05/08/2022</9>, there is increased <10>dilation of the pancreatic duct</10> upstream to the <11>ill-defined pancreatic mass</11>, now measuring <12>13 mm</12>, previously <13>8 mm</13>. The mass is partially obscured by the <14>biliary stent</14> and difficult to accurately measure/assess. 2.  Stable position of the <15>common bile duct stent</15>. There is mild <16>intrahepatic biliary ductal dilation</16> which is decreased compared to <17>05/08/2022</17>. There is also slightly more <18>pneumobilia</18>. Previously described <19>common bile duct thickening and enhancement</19> is less conspicuous on this exam. 3.  <20>Bilateral punctate renal calculi</20> without <21>hydronephrosis</21>. Report dictated by: ***** ***** *****, MD, signed by: ***** ***** *****, MD Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging    <22>CT Chest with Contrast</22>    Result Date: <23>06/23/2022</23>  <24>CT CHEST WITH CONTRAST</24> CLINICAL HISTORY:  <25>Pancreatic cancer</25>, primary restaging scan COMPARISON: <26>CT</26> <27>04/29/2022</27> TECHNIQUE: Serial <28>1.25 mm axial images</28> through the chest were obtained after the administration of <29>intravenous contrast</29>. <30>Iohexol 350</30> - <31>100 mL</31> - <32>Intravenous</32> RADIATION DOSE INDICATORS: ***** *****: <33>7</33> , <34>CTDIvol Min</34>: <35>4.4 mGy</35>, <36>CTDIvol Max</36>: <37>8.3 mGy</37>, <38>DLP</38>: <39>1065.2 mGy.cm</39>. The following accession numbers are related to this dose report *****,***** FINDINGS: <40>LUNGS</40>: No nodules. <41>PLEURA</41>: No effusions. <42>MEDIASTINUM</42>: No lymphadenopathy. <43>HEART</43>/***** *****: Normal size chambers and vessels. <44>Scattered coronary atherosclerosis</44>. <45>BONES/SOFT TISSUES</45>: No suspicious lesions. VISIBLE <46>ABDOMEN</46>: Please see dedicated <47>Abdomen and Pelvis CT report</47>.No evidence of <48>metastatic disease</48> in the chest. Report dictated by: ***** ***** *****, MD, signed by: ***** *****
