temperature source <1>Oral</1>, resp. rate <2>14</2>, height <3>177.8 cm</3> (<4>5' 10"</4>), weight <5>69.9 kg</5> (<6>154 lb</6>), <7>SpO2 96 %</7>. General appearance: No acute distress, conversant, appropriately interactive. Non-toxic, well-appearing. Eyes: <8>anicteric sclerae</8>, <9>moist conjunctivae</9>; no lid lag. HEENT: <10>Atraumatic</10>; <11>oropharynx clear</11> with <12>moist mucous membranes</12> and no <13>mucosal ulcerations</13>; normal hard and soft palate Neck: <14>Full range of motion</14>, <15>supple</15>, no <16>lymphadenopathy</16> Lungs/respiratory: <17>Clear to auscultation</17>, with <18>normal respiratory effort</18> and no <19>intercostal retractions</19> Cardiovascular: <20>RRR</20>, <21>normal S1 S2</21>, no <22>murmurs</22>, <23>gallops</23>, or <24>rubs</24>. Abdomen/GI: <25>Soft</25>, <26>non-tender</26>, <27>nondistended</27>; no <28>masses</28>, <29>ascites</29>, or <30>hepatomegaly</30>. <31>Tympanitic to percussion</31>. Back: No <32>point spinal tenderness</32>. Extremities: No <33>peripheral edema</33> or <34>discoloration</34> palpated or visualized. Skin: <35>Normal temperature</35>, <36>turgor</36> and <37>texture</37>; <38>scattered crusty lesions</38> on <39>forehead</39>, <40>scalp</40> Neuro: <41>Normal bulk</41>, <42>tone</42>, and <43>strength</43> in <44>upper and lower extremities</44>. <45>Intact gait</45>. No <46>focal sensorimotor deficits</46>. Psych: <47>Appropriate affect</47>, <48>alert</48> and <49>oriented</49>.
``` 
