Impression and Recommendations:  In summary, Ms. ***** is a 69 y.o. female with <1>metastatic pancreatic cancer</1>, currently receiving study on our *****-002 <2>chemotherapy/immunotherapy clinical trial</2>. Clinically she appears well enough, and <3>laboratory parameters</3> are acceptable, to proceed with her next dose of treatment today (Cycle 2 day 1), consisting of the combination of <4>gemcitabine</4> plus *****-<5>paclitaxel</5> at unchanged full doses.     We will plan to <6>reimage</6> her following cycle #2 to formally assess <7>treatment response/disease control</7>; additionally, per protocol, she will undergo repeat <8>tumor biopsy</8> (likely of the <9>primary pancreatic tumor</9>, via <10>EUS</10>)  during cycle #2 for research *****.    Return to clinic: 1 week     I spent a total of 25 minutes face-to-face with the patient and 25 minutes of that time was spent counseling regarding the <11>treatment plan</11>, <12>lifestyle modification</12> and <13>symptoms</13>    ***** *****, NP    
``` 
