require consideration of further treatment. I will go ahead and order him for f/u <1>CT scans</1> again in 3 months' time, at which point he can also have repeat <2>labs</2> inc <3>*****-9</3> checked. At a point where he needs to resume therapy down the road, either <4>*****</4> with <5>gemcitabine</5>/<6>*****-paclitaxel</6>, or exploring experimental clinical trial options, would be appropriate to consider. Of note, we do still have open here at <7>*****</7> a randomized phase II trial evaluating <8>CRS-207</8> for <9>chemotherapy refractory *****</9>, which is an attenuated mesothelin-expressing <10>Listeria vaccine</10>. On this study, patients are randomized to either <11>CRS-207</11> alone, <12>CRS-207</12> in combination with <13>*****</13>, or standard single-agent chemotherapy [<14>gemcitabine</14>, <15>capecitabine</15>, <16>5-*****</16>, <17>irinotecan</17>, or <18>erlotinib</18>]). He may represent a good candidate for this study if he is interested. All of the patient's questions were answered to his satisfaction. Overall, I am very pleased and impressed with how he is doing at this point.
