visit related to overall decline. Since ***** <1>gemcitabine</1> he has had a marked decline. He is spending most of the day in bed and gets out of bed at around 12pm or 1pm. He then manages to sit up on the couch for part of the day before returning to bed. Needs assistance with getting out of bed. Not eating very much due to <2>altered taste sensation</2>, <3>poor appetite</3>, and <4>early satiety</4>. <5>Abdominal distension</5> has increased and he is feeling more uncomfortable. He denies any acute <6>pain</6>, <7>fevers</7>, <8>chills</8>, <9>falls</9>, <10>constipation</10>, <11>diarrhea</11>, <12>nausea</12>, <13>emesis</13>. REVIEW OF SYSTEMS: 14 point ROS completed and all other systems were reviewed and are negative. Current Outpatient Medications Medication Sig Dispense Refill enoxaparin (<14>LOVENOX</14>) <15>60 mg/0.6 mL injection</15> Inject <16>0.6 mL</16> (<17>60 mg</17> total) under the skin every 12 (twelve) hours. <18>60 Syringe</18> 3 levothyroxine <19>50 mcg tablet</19> Take 1 tablet (<20>50 mcg</20> total) by mouth Daily. <21>30 tablet</21> 0 ondansetron (<22>ZOFRAN</22>) <23>8 mg tablet</23> Take 1 tablet (<24>8 mg</24> total) by mouth every 8 (eight) hours as needed for <25>Nausea</25>. <26>15 tablet</26> 1 prochlorperazine (<27>COMPAZINE</27>) <28>10 mg tablet</28> Take 1 tablet (<29>10 mg</29> total) by mouth every 6 (six) hours as needed (<30>nausea and vomiting</30>). <31>20 tablet</31> 0 lipase-protease-amylase (*****) <32>25,000-79,000-105,000 unit CAPDREC</32> Take <33>75,000 Units</33> by mouth 3 (three) times daily with meals. Take <34>3 capsules</34> by mouth 3 (three) times daily with meals (Patient not taking: Reported on 05/06/2019) <35>270 capsule</35> 3 LORazepam (<36>ATIVAN</36>) <37>1 mg tablet</37> Take 1/2 tab to 1 tab at night. For <38>insomnia</38> and <39>anxiety</39> <40>30 tablet</40> 1 No current facility-administered medications for this visit.
