Eventually the <1>pain</1> resolved and because of the long wait in the <2>ED</2> he left *****. <3>Chest x-ray</3> done at that time was unremarkable. His <4>chest CT</4> at one point suggested multiple new <5>pulmonary nodules</5> but he had evidence of good <6>tumor</6> control with a decreasing size of <7>mass</7> in the <8>pancreas</8> and a falling <9>CA-19-9</9>. He did see a <10>pulmonologist</10> who felt that these were inflammatory in nature and should be observed. He had an episode of <11>bursitis</11> in his <12>L elbow</12> which is now resolved. He completed <13>4 cycles of therapy</13>. On June 21, he underwent a <14>distal pancreatectomy</14>, <15>en bloc splenectomy</15> and <16>en bloc resection of the portal vein</16>. <17>Pathology</17> revealed a <18>moderately differentiated adenocarcinoma</18> with <19>1 of 13 lymph nodes positive</19>. <20>Margins</20> were negative. Following <21>surgery</21>, he received his final <22>2 cycles of gemcitabine</22> and <23>Abraxane</23>. After completing <24>treatment</24>, he experienced a <25>DVT</25> and he resumed <26>Lovenox therapy</26>. He has completed a <27>3 month course</27>. Eventually, he began to have some mild <28>back pain</28>. <29>CT scan</29> revealed a <30>soft tissue mass</30> around the <31>celiac access</31> and <32>adenopathy</32>. He underwent an <33>EUS guided biopsy</33> and this revealed <34>adenocarcinoma</34>. We then elected to resume <35>chemotherapy</35> but switched to reduced dose *****. He did not tolerate this well. After <36>8 cycles</36>, he had stable <37>disease</37> in the <38>abdomen</38> but progressing <39>pulmonary metastases</39> and we decided to give him a <40>chemotherapy holiday</40>. When we saw him in October 2016, he was having progressive <41>disease</41>. We elected to start <42>gemcitabine</42> and <43>Abraxane</43>. He has now had almost <44>4 cycles</44>. He is scheduled for <45>day 15 cycle 4</45> today. He is coming in to discuss his overall <46>management</46> and he is very worried about his upcoming <47>scan</47>. He is <48>depressed</48> but is now on <49>Effexor</49>. His <50>energy level</50> is decreased but he thinks this is a bit better on <51>ginseng</51> and he is going to restart his <52>Ritalin</52>. He does have some mild <53>neuropathy</53> and this ***** some with his <54>fine motor skills</54> but he is
