 further worked up with <1>endoscopic ultrasound</1>. 2.  No arterial vascular involvement. Slight contour flattening/mass effect on the posterior aspect of the <2>superior mesenteric vein</2> where it crosses the <3>uncinate process</3>; if malignancy is present, this would constitute <4>tumor abutment</4>. 3.  No definite evidence of <5>metastatic disease</5> in the <6>abdomen</6> or <7>pelvis</7>. 4.  <8>Aneurysmal dilatation</8> of the <9>infrarenal abdominal aorta</9> measuring <10>4.7 cm</10>, similar to prior. 5.  Nonspecific diffuse wall thickening of the <11>distal esophagus</11>, possibly representing <12>esophagitis</12>. Report dictated by: ***** *****, MD, signed by: ***** ***** *****, MD Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging    <13>Ct Chest With Contrast</13>
``` 
