ASSESSMENT & PLAN  In summary, ***** ***** ***** is a 71 y.o. male who presents to our <1>GI Oncology practice</1> at the <2>UCSF ***** ***** Family Comprehensive Cancer Center</2> for a follow-up visit of <3>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</3> s/p <4>distal pancreatectomy</4>. Pathology revealed <5>moderately differentiated adenocarcinoma</5> arising in association with an <6>intraductal papillary mucinous neoplasm</6> (gastric foveolar type, with moderate dysplasia) measuring <7>12 cm mass</7> in the <8>pancreatic body</8>. There was extension into the <9>peripancreatic soft tissues</9>, but is not identified at <10>surgical resection margins</10>. No <11>lymph nodes</11> were involved with cancer (0/32). He was started on <12>adjuvant therapy</12> with <13>gemcitabine</13> combined with <14>capecitabine</14> per the *****-4 trial (***** et al Lancet Oncology 2017) on <15>12/22/16</15>. Overall, he has been tolerating it well. His <16>scans</16> from <17>03/16/17</17> do not show any concerns of <18>recurrence</18>. His ***** was held due to <19>low ANC</19> (<20>0.2</20>) and he was given *****. We will plan to support him with <21>Neupogen</21> starting with this cycle. We are planning on <22>6 months</22> total of <23>adjuvant therapy</23>. We will proceed with ***** of <24>chemotherapy</24>.
``` 
