 today:  -<1>gemcitabine</1> <2>800 mg/m2</2> on days 1 and 8 (decreased due to <3>low ANC</3>)  -<4>capecitabine</4> <5>1500 mg po qam</5> and <6>2000 mg po qpm</6> on days January 22  cycle is <7>21 days</7>    -continue <8>Neupogen</8> <9>480 mcg</9> for <10>3 days</10> after infusion to help with <11>neutropenia</11>. If he does not feel well after <12>cycle 8</12>, we will not proceed with <13>cycle 9</13>. Otherwise, he will proceed with <14>cycle 9</14> and will leave for his trip on <15>06/13/17</15>.    -Monthly <16>CA 19-9 levels</16> have been <17>wnl range</17>. We will obtain <18>CT chest</18>, <19>abdomen</19> and <20>pelvis</20> after the completion of <21>adjuvant therapy</21>.    -After the <22>adjuvant therapy</22> has been completed, the patient's disease can be monitored with <23>surveillance CT scans</23> and <24>CA 19-9</24> every <25>3 months</25>.     -<26>Cancer Genetics appointment</26> was on <27>December 08</27>; results of the <28>genetic testing</28> are negative.    #<29>Prostate cancer</29>: <30>High-risk</30>, <31>September 29</31> cores positive, ***** <32>5+4</32>. He established care with Dr. ***** on <33>February 28</33> and started on <34>ADT therapy</34> with ***** on <35>02/28/17</35>.   -Plan for <36>surgical resection</36> in <37>September</37>.    #<38>Supportive care</38>: Patient has supply of <39>antiemetics</39>. I recommended that he continue to stay active and maintain his weight while undergoing therapy.     #<40>Goals of care</40>: <41>Curative</41>    #<42>Follow-up</42>: Patient will return to our clinic following his <43>restaging scans</43> via <44>telemedicine visit</44>. As always, we reminded the patient to call us with any questions or concerns in the meantime.    I spent a total of <45>25 minutes</45> face-to-face with the patient and <46>25 minutes</46> of that time was spent counseling regarding the <47>treatment plan</47>, <48>medication risks</48>, <49>lifestyle modification</49> and <50>symptoms</50>.      ***** *****, MD, MS  Clinical Assistant Professor of Medicine  Department of Medicine, Division of Oncology   UCSF ***** ***** Family Comprehensive Cancer Center  <51>05/12/2017</51>       
