*****. ***** is a 66 y.o. male with a new diagnosis of <1>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</1> with <2>biopsy</2>-proven <3>liver metastasis</3>. He is in excellent shape overall (<4>ECOG PS 0</4>) with minimal <5>cancer-related symptoms</5> at present. We discussed the details of his diagnosis and why the mainstay of treatment at this juncture should consist of <6>systemic therapy</6> with the goal of achieving as deep and durable a remission as possible, hopefully translating into significant prolongation of life, but that treatment was not expected to be curative. As such, it would be important to carefully weigh the risks/benefits of therapy and to prioritize ***** in the process. (Any consideration of <7>locoregional therapies</7> to the <8>pancreas</8> and/or <9>liver</9>, such as <10>radiation</10> or even <11>surgical resection</11>, are not appropriate at present but could conceivably be re-addressed down the road if he demonstrates a robust response w/durable disease control). In terms of standard of care options, there are several possible <12>chemotherapy regimens</12> to select from for <13>metastatic pancreatic cancer</13>, with the choice of therapy depending on the patient's age, performance status, co-morbid conditions, and personal preference; phase III evidence supports either ***** (biweekly ***** <14>5-*****</14>, <15>leucovorin</15>, <16>irinotecan</16>, and <17>oxaliplatin</17>) or the combination of <18>gemcitabine</18> plus *****-<19>paclitaxel</19> as appropriate front-line choices. We discussed the logistics, scheduling, and some of the potential side effects of these respective regimens including but not limited to <20>nausea/vomiting</20>, <21>alopecia</21>, <22>fatigue</22>, <23>cytopenias</23> with resultant <24>immunosuppression</24> and/or <25>anemia</25>, and <26>peripheral sensory neuropathy</26>/<27>cold sensitivity</27>. He appears well enough to go with *****, which I would recommend as his first line of therapy. In terms of front-line clinical trials for metastatic ***** at our institution: - Newly opened: A <28>Phase I trial</28> of <29>gemcitabine</29>/<30>*****-paclitaxel</30> plus *****-<31>030</31>, an <32>anti-CD39 antibody</32>
