Subjective:    This is a very pleasant 58-year-old gentleman with the aforementioned <1>diagnosis</1>. After having <2>right-sided abdominal pain</2> for about 3 months, he underwent a <3>CT scan</3> on October 22 that showed an ill-defined <4>mass in the pancreas</4>. This was followed by an <5>EUS with fine-needle aspirate</5> that recovered <6>adenocarcinoma</6>. On November 17, he underwent a <7>pancreatectomy</7> with <8>splenectomy</8>. <9>Pathology</9> showed <10>poorly differentiated adenocarcinoma</10> and measuring 5.0 x 5.0 x 4.0 cm. One of 25 <11>lymph nodes</11> were positive.    Postoperatively, he did quite well. When we initially saw him after surgery, he had evidence for a new solitary <12>liver met</12>. This was <13>biopsied</13> confirmed and he started on <14>treatment</14> with *****. He's completed 12 cycles and is now in treatment on a <15>clinical trial</15> of <16>maintenance chemotherapy</16> compared to <17>vaccine</17>. He was randomized to the <18>chemotherapy arm</18> and is on <19>capecitabine</19>. He has completed 3 cycles and is returning today for a followup <20>CT scan evaluation</20>.    He is having more <21>discomfort on the right side of his abdomen</21>. He occasionally takes <22>Tylenol</22> for this. Otherwise, his activity level and appetite is good. He's gained a kilogram. He denies any <23>nausea</23>. He has alternating <24>constipation</24> and <25>diarrhea</25>.   He has poor <26>stamina</26> during the second week of his <27>chemotherapy</27> with each cycle. He still has some <28>peeling on the bottom of his feet</28> and somewhat <29>tender to walk</29>.    <30>Medications</30> the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter.   <31>Medication</31> Sig    <32>ACETAMINOPHEN (TYLENOL ORAL)</32> Take 500 mg by mouth daily as needed.     <33>aspirin 325 mg EC tablet</33> Take 325 mg by mouth every 6 (six) hours as needed for <34>Pain</34>.    <35>calcium carbonate (TUMS) 200 mg calcium (500 mg) chewable tablet</35> Take 1 tablet by mouth 3 (three) times daily.    <36>capecitabine (XELODA) 150 mg tablet</36> Take 1 tab po QAM x 14 days on and 7 days off    <37>capecitabine (XELODA) 500 mg tablet</37> Take 2 tabs po QAM and 4 tabs po QPM x 14 days on and 7
