<1>Liver</1>:  A hypoattenuating lesion in <2>segment 7</2> has increased in size compared to the prior <3>CT</3>, now measuring up to <4>2.4 cm</4>, compared to <5>1.2 cm</5> previously. Other small subcentimeter hypodensities are grossly stable. These are most apparent in <6>segment 6</6>, where they measure up to <7>9 mm</7>.  <8>Gallbladder</8>:  Unremarkable   <9>Spleen</9>:  Surgically absent.  <10>Pancreas</10>:  Stable post operative changes related to resection of the <11>pancreatic body</11> and <12>tail</12>. There is stable ill-defined soft tissue thickening surrounding the <13>celiac axis</13>. No new soft tissue or mass in the <14>pancreatic bed</14>.  <15>Adrenal Glands</15>:  Unremarkable  <16>Kidneys</16>:  Unremarkable  <17>Vasculature</17>:  Unremarkable  <18>GI Tract</18>:  Unremarkable  <19>Pelvis</19>:  Unremarkable  <20>Lymphadenopathy</20>: Absent  <21>Ascites</21>: Absent  <22>Bones</22>:  No suspicious lesions     <23>11/23/2015</23>   <24>IMPRESSION</24>:  1.  Enlarging <25>hepatic metastasis</25> in <26>segment 7</26> of the <27>liver</27>, now measuring up to <28>2.4 cm</28> compared to <29>1.2 cm</29> previously. Other small nonspecific foci of hypoattenuation in the <30>liver</30> are stable. 2.  Stable postoperative changes related to a <31>distal pancreatectomy</31> with unchanged soft tissue surrounding the <32>celiac axis</32>. Continued attention on follow-up.  END OF <33>IMPRESSION</33>:
``` 
