SUBJECTIVE:    This is a very pleasant 77-year-old gentleman with a diagnosis of <1>adenocarcinoma of the pancreas</1> with <2>liver metastases</2>. He's been having intermittent <3>abdominal discomfort</3> and occasional <4>vomiting</4> since February of this year. He developed worsening <5>abdominal pain</5> in March and went to ***** ***** ***** Hospital where a <6>CT</6> was done. This showed a <7>hypodense mass</7> in the <8>head of the pancreas</8> measuring about 3 cm and numerous <9>hypodense lesions</9> in the <10>liver</10>. He also had an <11>incarcerated segment of small bowel</11> noted in the <12>left inguinal area</12>. A <13>core liver biopsy</13> was done which revealed <14>metastatic adenocarcinoma</14>, <15>CK 7</15> and <16>CK 20</16> positive. It was also noted that the <17>tumor</17> was <18>MSI high</18>.    He underwent an <19>inguinal hernia repair</19> for this on April 29 at *****.    We initially saw him about one month ago. At that time, he has mild <20>substernal discomfort</20> and just takes <21>extra strength Tylenol</21>. He had lost <22>12 pounds</22>. He had a very good appetite and he did not have <23>early satiety</23>. He was not sleeping well. He is normally quite active and plays golf and goes to the gym daily.    Because of his personal and family history, we were concerned that he may have a <24>hereditary susceptibility for cancer</24>. He was seen on the same date by <25>genetic counselors</25> and had <26>rapid testing for DNA pathway genes</26> and *****. These results were negative. The rest of his <27>genetic testing</27> is pending. As he had had a <28>core liver biopsy</28>, he was screened for the ***** trial but the material was insufficient for testing. He elected to start therapy with <29>gemcitabine</29> and <30>Abraxane</30>. He has now completed <31>2 cycles</31>.    His course has been complicated by a number of events. Just prior to starting his <32>chemotherapy</32>, he developed <33>biliary ductal obstruction</33>. An <34>ERCP</34> was done and <35>two metal stents</35> were placed. Just after starting his chemotherapy, he developed a symptomatic <36>DVT</36> and this was managed with therapeutic <37>Lovenox</37>. He continues on <38>anticoagulation</38>. Also on cycle 1
``` 
