ner_results: Mr. ***** is a 42 y.o. male who comes to our <1>GI Oncology practice</1> at the <2>UCSF Comprehensive Cancer Center</2> in consultation for his newly diagnosed <3>metastatic pancreatic cancer</3>. The history was obtained from the patient, along with my review of all his outside records. History of Present Illness This pleasant gentleman, previously entirely healthy, first noted <4>diffuse abdominal discomfort</4> a couple of months ago, with some accompanying <5>loss of appetite</5> and <6>10-lb weight loss</6>. These symptoms gradually progressed, prompting <7>diagnostic w/u</7> to be undertaken, including the following: - 09/21/2015: <8>3.3 x 2.9 x 3.3 cm pancreatic head mass</8> with associated <9>pancreatic duct dilatation</9>; <10>innumerable hepatic lesions</10> up to <11>4 cm in size</11>, some with small areas of probable <12>internal hemorrhage</12> with <13>compression of IVC and right renal artery and vein</13> - 09/23/2015: <14>EGD/EUS</14>: <15>Large 32.2 x 39.7 mm size pancreatic head mass</15>, associated with <16>small to large liver lesions</16> consistent with <17>metastatic disease</17> (*****, *****, <18>M1</18>). <19>FNA of both pancreatic mass and one liver lesion</19> c/w <20>adenocarcinoma</20>. The patient's present review of systems was reviewed and notable for the following: - <21>35-40 lb weight loss</21> in total - <22>Intermittent diarrhea</22> - <23>Some nausea</23> over past several days; <24>poor appetite</24> - <25>Generalized fatigue</25>; <26>ECOG PS 1</26> - <27>Generalized abdominal discomfort</27>; not requiring any <28>pain medications</28> - (+) <29>night sweats</29> - No <30>jaundice</30> - No <31>HAs</31> or <32>peripheral sensory neuropathy</32> - <33>Normal urination</33> - No <34>SOB/respiratory difficulties</34> - Some <35>reactive depression</35>. The remainder of a full review of systems was negative. Past medical history No chronic medical conditions. S/p <36>bilateral inguinal hernia repair</36> and <37>varicocele repair</37> in childhood. Outpatient Encounter Prescriptions as of 10/04/2015 Medication Sig Dispense Refill valACYclovir (<38>VALTREX</38>) <39>1 g tablet</39> Take <40>1,000 mg</40> by mouth every <41>12 (twelve) hours</41>. 
