well as extensive multifocal <1>hepatic metastases</1>. Impression and Recommendations: In summary, Mr. ***** is a 42 y.o. male with newly diagnosed <2>metastatic pancreatic cancer</2>. I explained to the patient and his family why the mainstay of treatment at this point should consist of <3>systemic therapy</3> rather than <4>surgery</4> or <5>radiation</5>, and that the goals of such treatment are to produce <6>disease control/remission</6> and hopefully extend survival, while possibly alleviating <7>cancer-related symptoms</7>, but that it is not curative in intent. There are several possible SOC <8>chemotherapy</8> options for <9>metastatic pancreatic cancer</9>, with the choice of therapy depending on the patient's age, performance status, co-morbid conditions, and personal preference. The two current gold standards for front-line treatment (for patients who are well enough to receive combination chemotherapy), based on phase III data, include: - ***** (biweekly ***** <10>5-*****</10>, <11>leucovorin</11>, <12>irinotecan</12>, and <13>oxaliplatin</13>), which was shown in a phase III French cooperative group trial to be superior to <14>gemcitabine monotherapy</14> for patients with <15>metastatic pancreatic cancer</15> in terms of <16>overall survival</16>, <17>PFS</17>, *****, and other clinical outcomes. Side effects of this regimen were discussed, including but not limited to <18>immunosuppression</18>, <19>risk of infection</19>, <20>hair loss</20>, <21>fatigue</21>, <22>nausea</22>, <23>vomiting</23>, <24>diarrhea</24>, and <25>peripheral sensory neuropathy</25>. I explained that this regimen requires placement of a <26>Mediport</26> due to the ***** component of therapy (48 hour infusion of <27>5-*****</27>). Furthermore, because of the high incidence of grade _ <28>neutropenia</28> with this regimen, we tend to give primary prophylaxis with <29>growth factor support</29> (***** or <30>Neupogen</30>) after each treatment cycle. - The combination of <31>gemcitabine</31> plus *****-<32>paclitaxel</32>, which was shown in a phase III international trial (*****) also to be superior to <33>gemcitabine monotherapy</33> for patients with <34>metastatic pancreatic cancer</34>
``` 
