<1>pancreatic cancer</1>. Side effects and logistics of this regimen were also explained. If Mr. ***** wishes to proceed with <2>SOC chemotherapy</2>, I would go the route of *****, and will try to help coordinate his <3>port placement</3> and initiation of treatment closer to home ASAP. Certainly <4>clinical trials</4> also represent an ideal option; we have two first-line trials here at ***** for which he may be eligible: - The ***** trial, a randomized phase II trial evaluating the combination of <5>gemcitabine</5> plus *****-<6>paclitaxel</6> with or without *****-*****, a bispecific monoclonal antibody directed against <7>IGF-1R</7> and *****. For this study, patients are initially screened by measurement of <8>serum free IGF-1 levels</8>, as only those with high <9>IGF-1 levels</9> are eligible. The patient was provided a consent form ahead of time to review and has a clear understanding of the experimental nature of this <10>clinical trial</10> and the essential logistics of the study. He went ahead and signed consent today, so we may proceed with initial screening and see if he qualifies. - We also have a second separate 1st-line trial evaluating the combination of <11>gemcitabine</11> plus *****-<12>paclitaxel</12> plus the <13>BTK inhibitor ibrutinib</13>, which he could consider if he does not qualify for the *****-***** trial by <14>serum IGF-1 level</14>. As the patient's wife was also very interested in learning about <15>clinical trials</15> using ***** as a <16>chemotherapy backbone</16>, I furthermore directed them to the ***** 1313 randomized phase II trial of ***** +/- the recombination <17>hyaluronidase enzyme</17> ***** that is ongoing in ***** and <18>USC</18>, although the logistics of travel and scheduling may make this prohibitive. Specifically, I do think it is imperative for Mr. ***** to get started on treatment sooner rather than later given his <19>symptoms</19> and burden of <20>disease</20>, so we will hopefully be able to move forward with one of the above options over the course of the next 1-2 weeks. In the meantime,
``` 
