Interval history/review of systems Due to evidence of some third-spacing, with <10>ascites</10> and a <11>R-sided pleural effusion</11>, she underwent both <12>paracentesis</12> (3400 cc) and <13>R-sided thoracentesis</13> (1000 cc) on 06/27/2016. <14>Cytology</14> from both of these fluid samples were benign. She is increasingly <15>fatigued</15> and far less active than previously. She denies any frank pain. She has developed some <16>jaundice symptoms</16>, with ***** and generalized <17>pruritis</17>. She may have had some transient relief from the perspective of her <18>breathing/cough</18> and <19>abdominal distention</19> post-procedure, but these symptoms have since recurred. She tried <20>Lasix</20> for one week, but self-d/c'ed this b/c it caused some <21>diarrhea</21> (since subsided). Appetite is sluggish. She denies any fevers/chills. 

Medications the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter. Medication Sig 
 <22>anastrozole (ARIMIDEX)</22> 1 mg tablet TAKE 1 TABLET EVERY DAY 
 <23>BYSTOLIC</23> 10 mg tablet TAKE 1 TABLET ORALLY EVERY DAY 
 <24>calcium carbonate (TUMS)</24> 200 mg calcium (500 mg) chewable tablet Take 1 tablet by mouth once as needed for <25>Heartburn</25>. 
 <26>fluticasone (FLONASE)</26> 50 mcg/actuation nasal spray 2 sprays by Nasal route Daily. 
 <27>furosemide</27> 
