SUBJECTIVE:  Mr. ***** is a 55 y/o man with a h/o <1>HTN</1> and a recent diagnosis of early stage <2>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</2> who is referred for evaluation of <3>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</3>.    Mr. ***** reports being in his usual state of health until the beginning of January when he started developing a <4>reduced appetite</4>, progressive <5>jaundice</5> and unintentional <6>weight loss</6> of about 20 pounds.  He presented to a local <7>ED</7> on February 19 and was found to have a  <8>Tbili</8> 9, <9>AST</9> 69, <10>ALT</10> 141, ***** 176.  ***** 02/18/18 <11>CT A/P</11> showed ***** and <12>extrahepatic ductal dilation</12>, <13>CBD</13> measuring 15 mm with an abrupt transition in <14>pancreatic head</14>, <15>dilated pancreatic duct</15> measuring up to 7 mm. This was concerning for underlying lesion such as a <16>mass at the head of the pancreas</16>. His <17>CA 19-9</17> was 24.  An <18>ERCP</18> was performed (report not available) and a <19>plastic biliary stent</19> was placed. <20>Brushings</20> were reportedly performed that did not show any malignancy (cytology report not available for review).  After stent placement his <21>Tbili</21> improved to 5.1 as of 02/20/18.    On 03/04/18 he underwent an <22>EUS</22> by Dr. *****, which demonstrated a <23>28 mm mass in the head of the pancreas</23> and <24>SMV</24>, a <25>dilated pancreatic duct</25> measuring 7mm with obstruction at the level of <26>pancreatic head mass</26>. A <27>FNA</27> of the <28>pancreas head mass</28> showed rare atypical cells in a background of <29>pancreatitis</29>.  Given high clinical suspicion for <30>pancreatic cancer</30>, he was referred for evaluation at ***** ***** *****. *****.  At his March 25 Dr. ***** appointment,  Dr. ***** reviewed his imaging and believed the mass is surgically resectable since there does not appear to be any <31>celiac</31> or <32>arterial</32> or <33>venous involvement</33>.  He recommended repeating imaging, a repeat <34>EUS</34> and <35>FNA</35> for tissue diagnosis at *****, and then <36>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</36> followed by <37>surgical resection</37>.    On 04/03/18 a <38>pancreatic protocol CT A/P</38> showed a <39>1.9 cm mildly hypodense mass in the pancreatic head</39>, with less than 180 degrees
