 of contact with the portal vein and mild focal contact with the superior mesenteric vein, and no arterial encasement.  A <1>CT Chest</1> did not show evidence of intrathoracic metastatic disease.  On 04/07/18 he underwent an <2>EUS</2> and <3>ERCP</3> with Dr. *****.  The <4>EUS</4> showed a <5>2.9 x 2.5 cm mass</5> in the <6>head of the pancreas</6> that involves the <7>pancreatic duct</7> and <8>bile duct</8> and appeared to involve the <9>splenoportal confluence</9>. Tissue was obtained for <10>cytology</10>.  <11>ERCP</11> showed <12>intrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation</12> with a <13>stricture of the common bile duct</13>. A <14>metallic stent</14> was deployed within the <15>common bile duct</15>.  Ultimately the <16>cytology</16> returned as positive for <17>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</17>, <18>MSS</18>.  The day following his <19>biopsy</19> he developed <20>severe abdominal pain</20> so on 04/08/18 he presented to an <21>OSH ED</21>. His <22>lab tests</22> revealed a mildly elevated <23>lipase</23> but no other significant abnormalities.  No imaging was performed.    Of note is his family history of <24>malignancy</24>.  His mother was diagnosed with <25>pancreatic cancer</25> at age 64, died 65.  Father diagnosed with <26>colon cancer</26> at 70.  His Maternal Grandmother had <27>colon cancer</27>.  Paternal aunt with <28>breast cancer</28>, died at age 37, and his paternal grandfather had <29>stomach cancer</29>.  He has had <30>germ line testing</30> and this was positive for <31>pathogenic APC mutation</31>.    We initially saw him in April 2018 and recommended therapy with <32>gemcitabine</32> and <33>Abraxane</33>. He experienced a delay in starting treatment because of <34>tumor ingrowth</34> into his <35>stent</35> which required revision. He also presented for his day 8 of his first cycle with <36>severe hypertension</36> and a <37>creatinine</37> of <38>3.59</38>. These problems eventually were controlled and he has completed <39>6 cycles of therapy</39>. His last <40>2 cycles</40> were given with <41>alternate week schedule</41> using <42>fixed dose rate gemcitabine</42>.    He was taken to <43>surgery</43> on 11/27/2018.He underwent a <44>portal vein resection</44>. <45>Path report</45> did show <46>residual adenocarcinoma</46>, <47>moderately differentiated</47>, with <48>8 of 23 lymph</48>
