   Immunohistochemistry was performed to evaluate the status of <1>DNA mismatch repair protein</1> expression on block A. The results in the <2>tumor cell nuclei</2> are:    ***** expression: Present.   ***** expression: Present.  ***** expression: Present.  ***** expression: Present.    Expression for all four markers, in most cases, indicates that the <3>DNA mismatch repair proteins</3> are intact. This result should be correlated  with the clinical presentation and family history to determine the need  for further work up for ***** syndrome.       ASSESSMENT:    1. <4>Adenocarcinoma</4> the <5>pancreas</5>. Status post <6>neoadjuvant therapy</6> with <7>gemcitabine</7> and <8>Abraxane</8> followed by <9>resection</9>  2. <10>ECOG 0</10>  3. <11>Hypertension</11>, better controlled  4. <12>APC mutation carrier</12>  5. Possible <13>local recurrence</13>    PLAN:    He may well have <14>local recurrence</14> but with the current <15>coronavirus crisis</15>, it will be difficult to work this up. As long as he is <16>asymptomatic</16>, we will watch this as hope that it represents delayed post op changes.    I performed this consultation using real-time <17>Telehealth tools</17>, including a live video connection between my location and the patient's location. Prior to initiating the consultation, I obtained informed verbal consent to perform this consultation using <18>Telehealth tools</18> and answered all the questions about the <19>Telehealth interaction</19>.    We'll see him again in 3 months for follow-up. I spent 20 minutes in face-to-face consultation with the patient today going over all aspects of his care and management.      
