ner_results: ```plaintext
 and negative margins.    <1>Imaging</1> since then have shown no recurrent <2>disease</2> in the <3>liver</3>, but slowly growing sub-cm <4>pulmonary nodules</4> (<5>right upper lobe</5> (6 x 6 mm), <6>right lower lobe</6> (8 x 10 mm)). She was seen by Dr. ***** ***** of our Thoracic Surgical faculty practice who took her for <7>robotic right thoracoscopic-assisted right upper lobe apical segment wedge resection</7> (0.6 cm) and <8>right lower lobe lateral/inferior basilar segment wedge resection</8> (0.1 cm) on <9>06/23/2018</9>; both of these specimens were c/w <10>metastatic adenocarcinoma</10>, with negative margins. Postoperatively, she did have a sizeable <11>R pleural effusion</11> requiring <12>thoracentesis</12> x 2 (<13>benign cytology</13>) that gradually resolved on its own.     After her operation, we opted for a period of time vigilant surveillance without immediate resumption of <14>systemic therapy</14>. However, her *****-9 levels gradually ***** upwards, with a <15>CT scan</15> performed here at ***** on <16>12/10/2018</16> showing growing tiny <17>pulmonary nodules</17> (sub-cm) as well as a slightly enlarging 1.3 cm <18>hypodense liver lesion</18>. On these bases, she resumed <19>chemotherapy</19> with the combination of <20>gemcitabine</20> plus *****-paclitaxel starting <21>01/06/2019</21>, on a planned ***** dosing schedule (days 1 and 15 of a 28-day cycle) with ***** <22>prophylaxis</22>. She continued treatment, aside from a 3-week treatment interruption early on for a ***** European cruise, through late May/early June, and was then taken back to the <23>O.R</23> at ***** ***** on <24>07/07/2019</24> for <25>wedge resection of her liver segment VIII metastasis</25> (1.3 cm <26>moderately differentiated adenocarcinoma</26> with negative margins). She made a very smooth postoperative recovery, and ultimately resumed <27>chemotherapy</27> with the same regimen as of <28>08/25/2019</28>.    Interval history/review of systems  Tolerating treatment without difficulty; energy level holding up well, with minimal cumulative <29>peripheral sensory neuropathy</29>. Appetite well-maintained, with only transient post-infusion <30>nausea</30>. Denies any intercurrent <31>fevers</31>, <32>chills</32>, or signs/symptoms of <33>infection</33>. No localizing <34>pain</34> aside from slight <35>abdominal discomfort</35> on occasion that is relieved with <36>BMs</36>. No <37>SOB</37>, <38>cough</38>, or <39>respiratory symptoms</39>.    The remainder of a full review of systems is negative.
