Ms. ***** is a 39 y.o. female who returns to our GI Oncology practice at the UCSF Comprehensive Cancer Center for follow-up of her <1>metastatic pancreatic cancer</1>.    History of Present Illness, reviewed:  This ***** with underlying <2>cystic fibrosis</2>(and ***** insufficiency *****-requiring <3>diabetes</3>)originally presented 2 weeks ago with <4>nausea</4>,<5>new-onset jaundice</5>,<6>RUQ/epigastric pain</6>,*****+lb <7>weight loss</7>(at initial onset, this was attributed to recently starting <8>Cymbalta</8>);as well as ***** <9>shortness of breath</9>, <10>chest tightness</10>,***** <11>sputum</11> c/f <12>cystic fibrosis exacerbation</12>. Initial diagnostic evaluation included <13>bloodwork</13> showing elevated <14>LFTs</14> (<15>alk phos</15> <16>1636</16>,<17>Tbili</17> <18>10.0</18> and <19>AST</19>/<20>ALT</20> *****/*****). In addition to <21>hepatitis w/u</21>, she ***** <22>abdominal CT scan</22> (08/12/2020) notable ***** <23>ductal obstruction</23> with truncation of the <24>common bile duct</24> at the level of the <25>pancreatic head</25>, as well as focal severe attenuation of the <26>main portal</26> ***** this same area, suspicious for a primary <27>pancreatic malignancy</27>.She then underwent *****/***** 08/13/2020, with placement of ***** <28>stent</28> through *****-<29>pancreatic biliary duct stricture</29>. <30>FNA</30> of the <31>pancreatic head</31> showed ***** for <32>adenocarcinoma</32>; repeat <33>EUS-FNA</33> on 08/21/2020 confirmed a diagnosis of <34>adenocarcinoma</34> involving the <35>pancreatic head</35>(as well as replacement of her <36>biliary stent</36> with a <37>metallic one</37>).    F/u <38>CT-PET</38> (08/21/2020) showed focal increased tracer uptake in the <39>pancreatic head</39> and neck measuring approximately <40>1.7 x 3.8 cm</40>, as well as a single mildly hypermetabolic <41>left neck base</41>, level 5 <42>lymph node</42> ***** <43>0.9 cm</43> possibly representing ***** <44>lymph node</44>(see formal report below).    She underwent an <45>U/S-guided LN biopsy</45> on 08/22/2020, which confirmed <46>metastatic adenocarcinoma</46>, consistent with <47>pancreas primary</47>.    Her treatment course to date:  - Initiated
