<1>chemotherapy</1> on 09/05/2020 with ***** cycle #1  - Admitted to ***** campus on 09/11/2020 with <2>cough</2>, <3>SOB</3>, and <4>fevers</4> at home c/w acute exacerbation of her <5>cystic fibrosis</5>, likely precipitated by inadequate <6>pulmonary toileting</6> at home. <7>Sputum cultures</7> were (+) for ***** <8>Achromobacter</8>, as well as a few <9>Aspergillus fumigatus</9>. <10>Rx'ed</10> with *****/***** in her hospital course, then d/c'ed to home on 09/17/2020 with <11>Zosyn</11> and <12>levaquin</12> for a 2 week course.  - Cycle #2 ***** 10/03/2020 with further reduction in <13>irinotecan</13> from 150 --> 120 mg/m2  - Second cycle generally better tolerated, with delayed <14>diarrhea</14> x 2 days, but she did subsequently require repeat hospital admission (October 15 - 10/23/2020) with severe <15>LLL MSSA pneumonia</15>/<16>bacteremia</16>. D/c'ed to home to ***** ***** <17>cefazolin</17> on 11/13/2020. Transferred <18>pulmonary/CF care</18> to <19>UCSF</19>, as well as <20>ID consultation</20> to provide recommendations re: <21>antibiotic/antifungal coverage</21> and monitoring.  - Received cycles 3 and 4 of ***** at unchanged doses, on schedule. Given (+) <22>respiratory symptoms</22> and <23>sputum cultures</23> from 11/15/2020 growing numerous <24>MSSA</24>, rare <25>Acinetobacter</25>, and moderate <26>Aspergillus</26>, following her most recent cycle (11/21/2020) she was started on a 2-week course of <27>IV cefazolin</27> (in ***** of her prophylactic <28>minocycline</28>) as well as <29>PO levofloxacin</29>, plus <30>TIW azithromycin</30>.    Interval history/review of systems  - <31>Respiratory symptoms</31>/<32>cough</32> somewhat improved over past couple of days, although she does also recent occasional <33>hot flashes</33>/<34>night sweats</34> (no <35>fevers</35>)  - <36>Chemotherapy</36> a/w modest <37>nausea</37>, well-controlled by <38>anti-emetics</38> with improvement of appetite after a few days  - Moderate <39>fatigue</39> (takes September 22 naps/day)  - Moderate <40>peripheral sensory neuropathy</40>/<41>cold sensitivity</41> that mostly dissipate by her off-week from treatment  - On stable dose of <42>long-acting morphine</42> (twice daily); <43>pain</43> well-controlled  - No <44>diarrhea</44>; <45>BMs</45> fairly  regular  - <46>Amenorrheic</46> since July 2020  - <47>Blood sugars</47> labile, esp while on <48>steroids</48> around the time of <49>chemotherapy</49>
