ner_results: ```plaintext
 recommended.    <1>CT abdomen with pancreatic protocol</1> was obtained on 11/25/15 showed the <2>pancreatic head mass</2> with abutment of the <3>superior mesenteric vein</3> with less than 90 degrees contact and probable preserved fat plane between the mass and vein. There was no contact with the <4>SMA</4>. There was additional 2.4 x 1.5 cm hypodense structure medial to the mass may represent a <5>metastatic lymph node</5> versus medial extension of the mass and abutment of the proximal <6>right renal artery</6>, with a preserved fat plane. There were additional prominent <7>periportal nodes</7> measuring up to 14 x 11 mm which were nonspecific. An enhancing lesion at the lateral interpolar region of the <8>right kidney</8> measuring 2.0 x 1.8 cm, suspicious for <9>renal cell carcinoma</9> was also noted.    She was evaluated by Dr. ***** who recommended <10>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</10>. She had <11>ERCP</11> with <12>biliary stent placement</12> on December 02.     *****/*****- *****/*****/*****: Admitted for <13>fever</13> with concern for potential <14>cholangitis</14>. <15>ERCP</15> wasn't performed.    *****/*****- *****/*****/*****: Admitted with <16>cholangitis</16>.  12/27/15: <17>ERCP</17> performed with purulent drainage noted for which small <18>sphincterotomy</18> was performed. Two double pigtail <19>stents</19> were placed in the bilateral ductal systems with good drainage. Discharged with 14 days of <20>antibiotics</20> (<21>ciprofloxacin</21> and <22>metronidazole</22>) with a repeat <23>ERCP</23> recommended in 4 weeks.     01/14/16: <24>C1D1</24> ***** (holding <25>irinotecan</25> due to <26>hyperbilirubinemia</26>)    01/24/16: <27>ERCP</27> revealed <28>suppurative cholangitis</28>, replaced one plastic <29>biliary stent</29> and admitted for <30>antibiotics</30> given the cholangitis. Noted a large area of <31>duodenum</31> ulcerated just distal to the bulb concerning for malignant invasion    01/28/16: <32>ERCP</32> when 2nd <33>stent</33> placed     02/03/16: <34>ERCP</34> revealed <35>duodenal narrowing</35> due to <36>tumor infiltration</36>. Previously placed plastic <37>stents</37> were removed.  High grade distal <38>CBD stricture</38> seen on <39>cholangiogram</39>. A 10 mm x 6 cm <40>Evolution uncovered metal biliary stent</40> was placed with good drainage. 
