Narrowing in <1>duodenum</1> noted without clinical signs of <2>gastric outlet obstruction</2> (if progression, enteral <3>stent</3> can be considered). 02/11/16: <4>Irinotecan</4> added with cycle 2 of ***** = ***** cycle 1 03/29/2016: <5>CT C/A/P</5> showed mild decreased size of ill-defined <6>pancreatic head mass</6> with decreased surrounding fat stranding and decreased size <7>lymph nodes</7> surrounding <8>pancreatic head</8> likely representing treatment response, unchanged 1.9 cm <9>R renal mass</9> concerning for <10>renal cell carcinoma</10>, no evidence of <11>metastatic disease</11> within <12>chest</12>. Scan reviewed by <13>surgeon</13> *****. *****, recommended 4 additional cycles due to ongoing abutment of <14>SMA</14> <180 degrees by <15>mass</15>. 04/05/2016: <16>CT chest</16> for <17>RUQ pain</17> with deep breaths ruled out *****. 04/19/2016: Cycle 7, Day 1 *****. <18>Platelets</18> = 94,000, <19>irinotecan</19> dose reduced 20%. 05/03/2016: <20>Chemotherapy</20> held for <21>platelets</21> = 76,000. 05/09/2016: <22>Platelets</22> = 59,000. Also recent <23>102F fever</23>, <24>chills</24>, <25>dark urine</25>. <26>T bili</26> = 3.7. <27>Blood cultures</27> negative. <28>Urine culture</28> positive for <29>Enterococcus</29>, started on <30>Cipro</30>. 05/09/2016: <31>US abdomen</31> showed ill-defined solid <32>mass</32> in region of <33>pancreas</33> with associated dilatation of <34>pancreatic duct</34>, metal <35>stent</35> within <36>common bile duct</36>, mild intrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation within <37>R and L lobes</37>, no sonographic evidence suggesting <38>cholecystitis</38>. 05/10/2016: <39>CT C/A/P</39> showed increased size of ill-defined <40>pancreatic head mass</40> with encasement of <41>gastroduodenal artery</41> by <42>mass</42>, 180 degree contact with irregular appearance of <43>superior mesenteric artery</43> suspicious for invasion, 90 degree contact with <44>superior mesenteric vein</44>, no definite evidence of <45>metastatic disease</45> in <46>chest</46>. 05/11/2016: <47>ERCP</47> - Narrowing and mild oozing of blood from <48>biliary tree</48> on cannulation suggested <49>tumor ingrowth</49>. 10 mm x 4 cm ***** fully covered <50>biliary stent</50> placed across <51>stricture</51>, within prior placed uncovered metal <52>stent</52>. 05/17/2016: Cycle 8, Day 1 *****
