<1>acute distress</1>, <2>ECOG 2</2>  Skin: No <3>rash</3>, <4>lesions</4>, <5>diaphoresis</5>, or <6>jaundice</6>.  Eyes: <7>PERRL</7>, <8>EOMI</8>, <9>anicteric sclera</9>.  HENT: <10>Moist mucous membranes</10>, <11>oropharynx clear</11> without <12>exudates</12> or <13>thrush</13>. <14>Alopecia</14>  Lymph Nodes: no <15>cervical lymphadenopathy</15>, <16>supraclavicular lymphadenopathy</16>  Respiratory:  <17>Good effort</17>, <18>clear to auscultation bilaterally</18>; no <19>wheezes</19>, <20>rales</20> or <21>rhonchi</21>.  Cardiovascular:  <22>Regular rate and rhythm</22>; no <23>murmurs</23>, <24>rubs</24>, or <25>gallops</25>.  GI: <26>Distended</26>, <27>shifting dullness</27>, <28>soft</28>, <29>bowel sounds normal</29>, <30>tenderness to palpation</30>, <31>palpable nodule in the LLQ</31> at the site of <32>prior paracentesis</32> (<33>1-2cm</33>)  Musculoskeletal: No <34>point tenderness</34> at <35>cervical spine</35>, <36>thoracic spine</36> or <37>lumbar spine</37>  Extremities: no <38>BLE edema</38>; no <39>cyanosis</39>  Neurologic:  <40>alert & oriented x 3</40>, <41>CN III-XII intact</41>, <42>ambulates w/o difficulty</42>; <43>October 07 BUE/BLE strength</43>    Diagnostic Data  <44>Labs</44>
