ner_results: ```plaintext
Subjective:    This is a very pleasant 79-year-old woman from ***** ***** presented with <1>nausea</1> in July and progressed to <2>abdominal pain</2>. She saw her <3>PCP</3> who ordered a routine <4>CT scan of the abdomen</4>. This showed small or dense lesions in the <5>head of the pancreas</5> and some prominence of the <6>pancreatic duct</6>. She was then referred to ***** ***** who performed an <7>EUS</7> and a <8>fine-needle aspiration</8> which confirmed <9>adenocarcinoma</9>. The <10>EUS</10> interpretation suggested that she had <11>SMA encasement</11>. The <12>biopsy</12> recovered a diagnosis of <13>adenocarcinoma</13>.  .  When we initially saw her in consultation, we were concerned that she might have <14>metastatic disease</14>. We did repeat a <15>pancreas protocol CT scan</15> and this confirmed a diagnosis of <16>locally advanced disease</16>. We started her on an alternate week fixed dose rate <17>gemcitabine</17> with <18>capecitabine</18>. She is now received two cycles. She initially had difficulty with <19>skin tenderness on her fingertips</19> and with <20>blisters on her lips</20> which were thought to be related to <21>herpes simplex</21>. She has been treated with <22>acyclovir</22>. However between the <23>lip blisters</23> and <24>tenderness in her fingertips</24>, she received incomplete dosing with <25>capecitabine</25> during her first cycle. Her second cycle, we reduced her <26>capecitabine</26> dose by 20%.     Despite this, she was still unable to complete her <27>capecitabine</27> during the third cycle and it was held on day 16.     Currently, her <28>abdominal pain</28> is well-controlled on <29>Norco</29>. She complains of a <30>low energy level</30> and <31>feeling cold all the time</31>. She still has some <32>peeling on her fingertips</32> especially in the flexor areas. She has some mild <33>nausea</33> which responds to <34>Zofran</34>. She has a good appetite. She has one to 2 soft formed <35>bowel movements</35> daily.    Since we last saw her, a <36>port</36> was placed.    Medications the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter.   Medication Sig    <37>coenzyme Q10</37> 100 mg capsule Take 300 mg by mouth Daily.    <38>HYDROcodone-acetaminophen (NORCO) 5-325</38>
``` 
