ner_results: ```plaintext
significant <1>FDG uptake</1>.. No hypermetabolic <2>lymphadenopathy</2>. Right chest wall <3>port</3> with <4>catheter tip</4> terminating in the lower <5>superior vena cava</5>. Abdomen/Pelvis: Redemonstrated ***** ill-defined <6>pancreatic neck mass</6> measuring approximately <7>2.4 cm</7>, which is grossly unchanged in size with a maximal <8>SUV</8> of <9>5.6</9>. Redemonstrated ***** appearance of the <10>mesentery</10> and mild <11>mesenteric adenopathy</11>, which may be secondary to vascular congestion; there is no significant uptake within scattered mesenteric borderline enlarged <12>lymph nodes</12>. Interval development of <13>ascites</13>, with mild free fluid in the pelvis which exhibits low level <14>FDG uptake</14> (maximal <15>SUV</15> <16>1.5</16>). There is an area of mild focal increased uptake which correlates to the <17>descending colon</17> and may relate to a <18>diverticulum</18>. Unchanged moderate <19>intrahepatic biliary and pancreatic ductal dilation</19>. Sequela of <20>superior mesenteric venous occlusion</20> from <21>tumor</21>, including <22>splenorenal shunt</22>, <23>gastric and paraesophageal varices</23>, and dilation of the <24>left gonadal vein</24>. <25>Diffuse anasarca</25>. Calcified <26>cholelithiasis</26>. Musculoskeletal: No metastatic disease. 1. No significant change in the <27>pancreatic neck mass</27> with ***** <28>SUV</28> <29>5.6</29>, with other abdominal findings which are grossly unchanged compared to 07/26/2015. 2. Interval development of a <30>right pleural effusion</30> and small to moderate free fluid in the pelvis both of which demonstrate low level <31>FDG uptake</31>. There is mild <32>peritoneal thickening</32>, though no definite soft tissue nodularity is seen. While the possibility of <33>malignant ascites</33> is a consideration though; for definitive evaluation, direct sampling may be considered if clinically indicated. This study was reviewed by attendings Dr. ***** ***** from ***** ***** and Dr. ***** ***** ***** of <34>Nuclear Medicine</34>. END OF IMPRESSION: Assessment: 1. <35>Adenocarcinoma of the pancreas</35>, <36>LAD</36>, with improved symptom control, no evidence of chemotherapy benefit based on <37>CA</37>
``` 
